moral authority there.

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:13.046
And it was perfect example
was when Trump finally...

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:17.017 align:start size:97% position:3%
When Syria crossed the red
line and did chemical weapons,

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:21.021
and Trump did the first shots
back and did the missiles,

00:00:21.021 --> 00:00:23.356
the number of ambassadors
that came to me and said,

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:25.859
it's so good to see the
United States lead again.

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:28.461
(upbeat music)

00:00:33.166 --> 00:00:36.736 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
- I am Dave Rubin and
believe it or not people,

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:40.740 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
I am live in studio
with a guest.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:43.710 align:start size:94% position:6%
She is the former governor
of South Carolina,

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:47.213 align:start size:84% position:16%
the former US
ambassador to the UN,

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:52.052
the author of the book right
here in my hands right now

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:53.286
and a real human being.

00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:54.220
I can't believe it, Nikki Haley.

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:55.488
- This is so fun.

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:56.656
It's so great to be with you

00:00:56.656 --> 00:00:58.058 align:start size:81% position:19%
thank you so much.
- Welcome.

00:00:58.058 --> 00:00:59.592 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, first, we just
gotta do this part.

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:02.195
I mean, we're sitting just a
few feet away from each other,

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:06.266 align:start position:0%
I have not done a live
interview in person since July.

00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:07.801
My last one was Ted Cruz,

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:09.569
So you gotta follow up Ted Cruz.

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:11.204
We'll see how that goes,

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:12.939 align:start size:84% position:16%
but just to sit
with another person.

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:15.041
- Oh, it's so nice, right?

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:16.309 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
I mean, we've been
through a lot.

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:17.777 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
The country's been
through a lot,

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:20.680 line:0%
but I think the country can't
wait to just be open again

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:24.250 align:start size:88% position:13%
and be moving and start
to live life again.

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:28.021 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Yeah, are you shocked
how long it's been?

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:29.722
I mean, a year and a half later,

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:32.525
it was two weeks to flatten
the curve and here we are.

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:34.327
- I mean, I think
if you had told us

00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:38.331
all of this was going
to happen prior to '20,

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:39.632
nobody would have believed it.

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:43.269
But to really see all
the forces at play,

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:45.772
the fear tactics, the idea that

00:01:45.772 --> 00:01:48.942 align:start size:84% position:16%
they keeping kids from
school, the masks,

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:52.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
just the over-exaggeration
of everything.

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:54.714
I hope it's taught
a lesson, which is,

00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:56.683
look, we all wanna
keep people safe.

00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:58.418
We all want to do our part.

00:01:58.418 --> 00:02:00.620
But there is a role
that government has

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:02.155 align:start size:88% position:13%
and there's a role that
government doesn't.

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:04.958
And the idea that
small businesses

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:07.827
that we lost thousands
of them through this.

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:09.629 align:start size:84% position:16%
The idea that people
were not allowed

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:11.231
to make their own decisions,

00:02:11.231 --> 00:02:12.565
that's a real mistake

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:14.367
and we shouldn't let
that happen again.

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:17.103
- So as a Conservative, do
you think in a weird way

00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:18.505
as terrible as this has all been

00:02:18.505 --> 00:02:20.039
this has been the best argument

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:22.308
for sort of small
government policies

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:23.943 align:start size:81% position:19%
that people are
kind of waking up.

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:26.212
Look, we're here at L.A
right now in California,

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:28.348 align:start size:84% position:16%
You know my feelings
about this place,

00:02:28.348 --> 00:02:31.484
that real world examples
have sort of led people,

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:34.988
I think, to fall more in
the Conservative bucket.

00:02:34.988 --> 00:02:35.955
- Look, I think we
have to see this

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:37.690
for the opportunity it is.

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:40.560
It was a reminder that
states should be able

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:44.230 align:start size:88% position:13%
to control what happens
in terms of laws.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.633
We don't need the federal
government mandating down.

00:02:46.633 --> 00:02:48.168
States know their people best,

00:02:48.168 --> 00:02:50.270 align:start size:84% position:16%
if you look at
whether it was Georgia

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:51.738
when they were the
first ones to open up

00:02:51.738 --> 00:02:53.072 align:start size:84% position:16%
and people were
screaming about it.

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:55.108 align:start size:84% position:16%
A governor knows where
their hotspots are.

00:02:55.108 --> 00:02:58.444
A governor knows which areas
they have to be careful of.

00:02:58.444 --> 00:03:00.613 align:start size:84% position:16%
So allowing governors
to decide that.

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:03.082
But if you look at the
states that stayed open,

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:05.585
versus the states
that closed down,

00:03:05.585 --> 00:03:08.087
you had more deaths in the
states that closed down.

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:10.757
I mean, there is something
to personal responsibility.

00:03:10.757 --> 00:03:12.158
And when I was governor,

00:03:12.158 --> 00:03:14.360
I always thought when
we had hurricanes,

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:17.597 align:start size:84% position:16%
you educate, you give
people the facts,

00:03:17.597 --> 00:03:19.799
then let them make
the best decision

00:03:19.799 --> 00:03:21.301
for them in their families.

00:03:21.301 --> 00:03:23.303
Government doesn't need to
make that decision for them.

00:03:23.303 --> 00:03:25.238
And this was a real
lesson during COVID

00:03:25.238 --> 00:03:28.408
of it does go too far.

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:30.143
And when you watch the economy

00:03:30.143 --> 00:03:31.411
and what we've been through

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:32.579
and the number of
people out of work

00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:33.880 align:start size:88% position:13%
and the small businesses
that have closed,

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:35.715
didn't have to happen that way.

00:03:35.715 --> 00:03:37.483
- Yeah, so you don't
think that governors

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:39.085
should just pick arbitrary dates

00:03:39.085 --> 00:03:41.120
like June 15th as Gavin Newsome

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:42.922
who is now being
recalled should do,

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:44.891
you don't think that
was the best idea?

00:03:44.891 --> 00:03:45.925
- I think it's pretty crazy.

00:03:45.925 --> 00:03:47.393
I mean, I really do.

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:48.962 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think that the idea
that, well, first of all,

00:03:48.962 --> 00:03:51.798
I think he knows a
recall is on the way.

00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:55.902 align:start size:84% position:16%
Shockingly California
needs to open up.

00:03:57.303 --> 00:04:00.506 align:start position:0%
No. I mean, I think, look,
people can make good decisions.

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:02.242 align:start size:84% position:16%
I still believe in the
goodness of people.

00:04:02.242 --> 00:04:04.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
I still believe that they
are perfectly capable

00:04:04.444 --> 00:04:06.813 align:start position:0%
of knowing what's best for their
children and their families

00:04:06.813 --> 00:04:08.381
and what they're willing to do.

00:04:08.381 --> 00:04:10.316
And government needs to
just move out of the way.

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:12.685
It's always been that way.

00:04:12.685 --> 00:04:14.087
I mean, people have to remember

00:04:14.087 --> 00:04:16.956
government breaks more
than it fixes always.

00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:18.191
- What did Ronald Reagan say?

00:04:18.191 --> 00:04:20.193 align:start size:81% position:19%
What was it the
worst eight words,

00:04:20.193 --> 00:04:21.227 align:start size:84% position:16%
I'm going to
slightly butcher it,

00:04:21.227 --> 00:04:22.161
I'm from the government

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:23.096
and I'm here to help you.

00:04:23.096 --> 00:04:24.330
Pretty much that's what...

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:26.532 align:start size:88% position:13%
Okay. I know we could
do, we could probably do

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:28.701
