00:08:53.900 --> 00:08:54.834
and all that stuff.

00:08:54.834 --> 00:08:56.068
But I thought for a second,

00:08:56.068 --> 00:08:57.136
we could just talk
a little bit about,

00:08:57.136 --> 00:08:58.838
just like your family history

00:08:58.838 --> 00:09:02.575 align:start size:97% position:3%
and just like the stuff that
people don't really know.

00:09:03.976 --> 00:09:06.546 align:start size:97% position:3%
So what's the Nikki Haley
story that people don't know.

00:09:06.546 --> 00:09:08.214
Give me the bio that
people don't know.

00:09:08.214 --> 00:09:10.049
- Born in South Carolina.

00:09:10.049 --> 00:09:13.419
Small rural town,
two stoplights.

00:09:13.419 --> 00:09:15.888 align:start size:88% position:13%
You couldn't think about
doing something wrong

00:09:15.888 --> 00:09:18.224
without somebody
telling your mom.

00:09:18.224 --> 00:09:21.894
We were the only Indian family
in that small Southern town.

00:09:21.894 --> 00:09:23.629
We weren't white
enough to be white,

00:09:23.629 --> 00:09:25.364
we weren't black
enough to be black.

00:09:25.364 --> 00:09:26.933 align:start size:84% position:16%
- And your parents
were first-generation.

00:09:26.933 --> 00:09:29.902
- Yes. My father wore turban,
he still does to this day.

00:09:29.902 --> 00:09:31.137
My mother wore a saree.

00:09:31.137 --> 00:09:32.572
They didn't know who
we were, what we were,

00:09:32.572 --> 00:09:34.106
while we were there.

00:09:34.106 --> 00:09:36.809
And I remember when I would
get teased on the playground

00:09:36.809 --> 00:09:38.678
and I would come home,

00:09:38.678 --> 00:09:40.880
my mom would say your
job is not to show them

00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:43.015 align:start size:88% position:13%
how you're different,
your job is to show them

00:09:43.015 --> 00:09:44.650
how you're similar.

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:46.686 line:0%
And it's amazing how
that lesson I learned

00:09:46.686 --> 00:09:48.988 line:0%
on the playground at five,

00:09:48.988 --> 00:09:51.591 line:0%
played out in my life
in the corporate world,

00:09:51.591 --> 00:09:53.559
as governor, as ambassador.

00:09:53.559 --> 00:09:55.561 align:start size:88% position:13%
Because when you're
faced with a challenge,

00:09:55.561 --> 00:09:58.531
if you first talk about the
things you have in common,

00:09:58.531 --> 00:10:00.600
everybody lets their guard down.

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:03.836 align:start size:97% position:3%
Then you can go in and
start working on a solution.

00:10:03.836 --> 00:10:08.841
- Yeah. So technically you
are a brownish skinned woman,

00:10:10.109 --> 00:10:13.446 align:start position:0%
but you are a scary
Conservative to the mainstream.

00:10:13.446 --> 00:10:15.214
Do you find that frustrating,

00:10:15.214 --> 00:10:18.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you don't get that
little bit of bonus credit

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:21.220 align:start size:97% position:3%
that they might give to
you if you were a Democrat?

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:22.688
- It's always kinda been tough.

00:10:22.688 --> 00:10:25.725
When I was elected governor
there was a Conservative

00:10:25.725 --> 00:10:27.994
that called me a rag head,
and there was a Democrat

00:10:27.994 --> 00:10:30.162
that said I was just a
Conservative with a tan.

00:10:30.162 --> 00:10:33.299
I mean, it's never
enough for anyone

00:10:33.299 --> 00:10:35.801 align:start size:88% position:13%
but the thing is
minorities in particular

00:10:35.801 --> 00:10:38.938 align:start size:88% position:13%
get really offended
when there's a minority

00:10:38.938 --> 00:10:40.306
that's a Conservative.

00:10:40.306 --> 00:10:44.110
And so yeah, we fight
battles from all sides.

00:10:44.110 --> 00:10:46.212
But at the end of the day, you
have to stay true to yourself

00:10:46.212 --> 00:10:48.314
and you have to talk
about what you believe

00:10:48.314 --> 00:10:50.716 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I feel like
that through my life

00:10:50.716 --> 00:10:54.487
even though there's been
hate from different sides,

00:10:54.487 --> 00:10:57.857
if you push for the right
thing people see that.

00:10:57.857 --> 00:11:00.326 align:start size:97% position:3%
- So you think that American
dream, it kind of works

00:11:00.326 --> 00:11:01.727
if you play by the rules.

00:11:01.727 --> 00:11:02.962
- It's why I get so upset

00:11:02.962 --> 00:11:04.797
when they say we're
a racist country.

00:11:04.797 --> 00:11:07.967
I mean, did we have racial
issues when I was growing up?

00:11:07.967 --> 00:11:10.703
Yes, but that's the same state

00:11:10.703 --> 00:11:12.938
that allowed my dad
to be a professor.

00:11:12.938 --> 00:11:14.940
That's the same state
that supported my mom

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:16.442
and her small business.

00:11:16.442 --> 00:11:18.344
It's the same state that
allowed me to be governor.

00:11:18.344 --> 00:11:20.946 align:start position:0%
You know, it's the country that
allowed me to be ambassador

00:11:20.946 --> 00:11:23.482 align:start size:88% position:13%
and I'm one of millions
of cases like that

00:11:23.482 --> 00:11:26.419
where only in this
country can you do

00:11:26.419 --> 00:11:28.521 align:start size:88% position:13%
or be anything you want
to be in government

00:11:28.521 --> 00:11:29.822
will stay out of your way.

00:11:30.956 --> 00:11:32.491
- At least for now.

00:11:32.491 --> 00:11:34.560
- We have to make
sure we're always.

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:37.229
But you know even being
at the United Nations,

00:11:37.229 --> 00:11:39.799
there's something amazing
when countries would come

00:11:39.799 --> 00:11:43.002
and be amazed at how we
had freedom of speech

00:11:43.002 --> 00:11:47.106
and freedom of religion and
the opportunities awarded

00:11:47.106 --> 00:11:48.974
regardless of where you
were born and raised,

00:11:48.974 --> 00:11:50.276
that's special.

00:11:50.276 --> 00:11:52.078
And that's why it
bothers me so much

00:11:52.078 --> 00:11:53.679
when people criticize America.

00:11:53.679 --> 00:11:58.451
We are the best country
in the world hands down,

00:11:58.451 --> 00:12:00.152
and we have to fight for Her.

00:12:00.152 --> 00:12:01.554
It's worth fighting for.

00:12:01.554 --> 00:12:03.355
Because when you see
the countries I've seen

00:12:03.355 --> 00:12:05.658
and you've been the
places I've been,

00:12:05.658 --> 00:12:08.060
you'd never complain
again if you saw them.

00:12:08.060 --> 00:12:10.162
- Are you shocked that it
feels like so many people

00:12:10.162 --> 00:12:12.932
are kind of folding right
now and just being like,

00:12:12.932 --> 00:12:17.670
oh, this thing, whatever
it is, woke-ness, Marxism,

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:20.206 align:start size:97% position:3%
Cancel culture, it's just
encroaching and encroaching,

00:12:20.206 --> 00:12:22.441
and it doesn't seem like a
lot of people are fighting

00:12:22.441 --> 00:12:23.909 align:start size:88% position:13%
and you've been fighting
for a long time,

00:12:23.909 --> 00:12:25.578
and we'll get to the UN
stuff in a little bit.

00:12:25.578 --> 00:12:27.113
- I wish they could
see what I've seen.

00:12:27.113 --> 00:12:29.682 align:start size:97% position:3%
If you've been to the
Democratic Republic of Congo,

00:12:30.883 --> 00:12:32.218
where they use rape
as a weapon of war,

00:12:32.218 --> 00:12:33.619
when you've been to South Sudan

00:12:33.619 --> 00:12:35.454 align:start size:84% position:16%
where I've sat
with crying mothers

00:12:35.454 --> 00:12:37.356 align:start size:84% position:16%
whose babies were
taken from their arms

00:12:37.356 --> 00:12:38.824
and thrown into fires.

00:12:38.824 --> 00:12:40.392
When you've been on the
Simon Boulevard Bridge

00:12:40.392 --> 00:12:43.195 align:start size:81% position:19%
watching thousands
of Venezuelans

00:12:43.195 --> 00:12:46.499
holding the babies in their
hands for hours in the sun

00:12:46.499 --> 00:12:49.368
to go get the one meal
they might get that day.

00:12:49.368 --> 00:12:52.471 align:start size:97% position:3%
My husband's a combat veteran,
he served in Afghanistan,

00:12:52.471 --> 00:12:54.573
and he said, I wish
people in America

00:12:54.573 --> 00:12:57.576
could just spend one
day in Afghanistan.

00:12:57.576 --> 00:13:00.679 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because even the homeless
here have it better

00:13:00.679 --> 00:13:02.448 align:start size:84% position:16%
than what they have
in Afghanistan.

00:13:02.448 --> 00:13:04.183
That's what I want
people to remember

00:13:04.183 --> 00:13:09.188
is even on our worst day, we
are blessed to live in America.

00:13:10.055 --> 00:13:11.323
- Do you sense we're suffering

00:13:11.323 --> 00:13:12.525
from our own success
in a weird way then?

00:13:12.525 --> 00:13:14.593 align:start size:84% position:16%
- I think we're taking
a lot for granted.

00:13:14.593 --> 00:13:18.464 align:start size:97% position:3%
There's a reason if you
speak with legal immigrants,

00:13:18.464 --> 00:13:21.066
they are in some ways
so much more patriotic

00:13:21.066 --> 00:13:22.401
than people that were born here.

00:13:22.401 --> 00:13:23.636
Because they get it,

00:13:23.636 --> 00:13:25.304 align:start size:81% position:19%
they get what's
on the other side.

00:13:25.304 --> 00:13:28.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
What I want us to remember
is we're not perfect,

00:13:28.574 --> 00:13:30.276
we're a work in progress.

00:13:30.276 --> 00:13:33.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
But we've gotten it better
than any other country.

00:13:33.712 --> 00:13:36.816
And the second you
let this woke culture

00:13:36.816 --> 00:13:40.085
and this cancel culture
start bullying people out

00:13:40.085 --> 00:13:42.154
of what they believe
and what they think

00:13:42.154 --> 00:13:44.490
and what they want
to do to succeed,

00:13:44.490 --> 00:13:46.525 align:start size:81% position:19%
don't tear down
the one part of us

00:13:46.525 --> 00:13:49.695
that's so great that other
countries envious for it.

00:13:49.695 --> 00:13:51.597
- And yet here we are.

00:13:51.597 --> 00:13:53.032
- And we're here.

00:13:53.032 --> 00:13:54.533
And you know what?

00:13:54.533 --> 00:13:58.470 align:start position:0%
This elections have consequences
and we're feeling the burn.

00:13:58.470 --> 00:14:01.907
But sometimes you have to feel
the burn to know where up is.

00:14:01.907 --> 00:14:03.909
And we got to start looking up,

00:14:03.909 --> 00:14:05.144
we got to start pulling out.

00:14:05.144 --> 00:14:07.079 align:start size:81% position:19%
And this is not
the time to whine,

00:14:07.079 --> 00:14:09.415
this is not the time to
complain or get lazy,

00:14:09.415 --> 00:14:10.649
this is a time to fight.

00:14:10.649 --> 00:14:12.484
This is the time we fight back,

00:14:12.484 --> 00:14:15.654
we push back for what we
believe in and be proud.

00:14:15.654 --> 00:14:19.325 align:start size:97% position:3%
Be proud of this country
because it's given us so much

00:14:19.325 --> 00:14:20.759 align:start size:88% position:13%
and there's so much
more it's going to give

00:14:20.759 --> 00:14:22.528
our kids and our grandkids.

00:14:22.528 --> 00:14:24.063
- All right.

00:14:24.063 --> 00:14:25.798
So that probably could have
been your closing statement

00:14:25.798 --> 00:14:27.600
but I'm not letting
you out that easy.

00:14:27.600 --> 00:14:30.135
So let's back up
for a little bit.

00:14:30.135 --> 00:14:32.104
When did you decide
to go into politics

00:14:32.104 --> 00:14:33.339
and I guess more importantly,

00:14:33.339 --> 00:14:34.940
why did you decide
to go into politics?

00:14:34.940 --> 00:14:36.742 align:start size:81% position:19%
- I was never that
political kid.

00:14:36.742 --> 00:14:38.744
I never cared about politics,

00:14:38.744 --> 00:14:41.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
in high school I was never
in student government,

00:14:41.614 --> 00:14:43.549
not in college Republicans.

00:14:43.549 --> 00:14:45.718
I had started doing the books

00:14:45.718 --> 00:14:48.754 align:start size:84% position:16%
for my family business
when I was 13.

00:14:48.754 --> 00:14:52.024
And didn't know that wasn't
normal until I to college.

00:14:52.024 --> 00:14:55.094
But really when
times were tough,

00:14:55.094 --> 00:14:56.528
I learned how to
stretch a dollar,

00:14:56.528 --> 00:14:57.696
I had to figure out
what we're going

00:14:57.696 --> 00:14:59.331
to pay and what we weren't,

00:14:59.331 --> 00:15:01.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
and when times were good,
we never celebrated.

00:15:01.200 --> 00:15:03.769
Because you knew bad times
were going to happen again.

00:15:03.769 --> 00:15:06.739
Ended up going to
Clemson, go tigers,

00:15:06.739 --> 00:15:08.440 align:start size:84% position:16%
graduated with a
degree in accounting

00:15:08.440 --> 00:15:13.212
and then worked for a company
in six of its subsidiaries

00:15:13.212 --> 00:15:14.680
as the accounting supervisor,

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:17.549 align:start position:0%
and then I got tired of working
for the guys down the hall.

00:15:17.549 --> 00:15:20.152
And so we came back home
to the family business.

00:15:20.152 --> 00:15:22.421 align:start size:84% position:16%
And one day I was
complaining to my mom

00:15:22.421 --> 00:15:24.990 align:start size:84% position:16%
about how hard it
was to make a dollar

00:15:24.990 --> 00:15:28.027
and how easy it was for
government to take it.

00:15:28.027 --> 00:15:29.762
And she said, quit
complaining about it

00:15:29.762 --> 00:15:31.330
do something about it.

00:15:31.330 --> 00:15:33.165 align:start size:88% position:13%
I did not know you
weren't supposed to run

00:15:33.165 --> 00:15:35.034
against a 30 year old
in Congress primary.

00:15:35.034 --> 00:15:37.670 align:start size:84% position:16%
I truly didn't,
ignorance is bliss.

00:15:37.670 --> 00:15:42.041
But once I realized he was
related to half the district,

00:15:42.041 --> 00:15:44.510
and I had thrown my head in,
the only option was to win.

00:15:44.510 --> 00:15:46.512
So my husband got in
the driver's seat,

00:15:46.512 --> 00:15:47.780
I was in the passenger seat,

00:15:47.780 --> 00:15:49.248
we put our two little
ones in the back seat

00:15:49.248 --> 00:15:50.749
and I started knocking on doors

00:15:50.749 --> 00:15:53.419 align:start size:84% position:16%
and was able to win
that state house seat.

00:15:53.419 --> 00:15:56.822 align:start position:0%
And truly it was, I thought
there were way too many lawyers

00:15:56.822 --> 00:15:59.591 align:start position:0%
at the state house and they
needed a really good accountant.

00:15:59.591 --> 00:16:01.560
- Yeah. So then that
was just the beginning

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:02.861
of your political
career, really.

00:16:02.861 --> 00:16:05.097
So when did you decide
to take the next step?

00:16:05.097 --> 00:16:07.232
- So interestingly enough,

00:16:07.232 --> 00:16:10.169
in South Carolina,
legislative votes,

00:16:10.169 --> 00:16:12.972 align:start size:88% position:13%
they counted legislative
votes by voice vote,

00:16:12.972 --> 00:16:17.977
all in favor, say, aye, all
oppose, the ayes have it.

00:16:19.178 --> 00:16:20.479
But one day there was
a piece of legislation

00:16:20.479 --> 00:16:21.613
that was right across the desk

00:16:21.613 --> 00:16:24.049 align:start size:88% position:13%
that would give
legislators pay raises.

00:16:24.049 --> 00:16:27.052
All in favor say aye,
all opposed silence,

00:16:27.987 --> 00:16:29.488
and they passed it

00:16:29.488 --> 00:16:31.123
and yet to this day, you
can't find one legislator

00:16:31.123 --> 00:16:33.592
that said they voted
themselves a pay raise.

00:16:33.592 --> 00:16:34.827
- You don't say.

00:16:34.827 --> 00:16:36.862
- Republican house,
Republican Senate,

00:16:36.862 --> 00:16:39.064 align:start size:88% position:13%
I went to our Republican
speaker of the house

00:16:39.064 --> 00:16:41.700
and I said this is why
people don't trust us.

00:16:41.700 --> 00:16:44.636
And I filed some legislation

00:16:44.636 --> 00:16:46.171
that said anything
important enough

00:16:46.171 --> 00:16:48.674
to be debated on the floor
of the house or the Senate

00:16:48.674 --> 00:16:52.044
is important enough for people
to have votes on the record.

00:16:52.044 --> 00:16:54.213
So the speaker pulled me aside

00:16:54.213 --> 00:16:56.115
and he said put the bill away,

00:16:56.115 --> 00:16:57.316
we don't need to have it,

00:16:57.316 --> 00:16:59.118 align:start size:88% position:13%
we will decide what
the public needs to see

00:16:59.118 --> 00:17:00.652
and what they don't.

00:17:00.652 --> 00:17:03.255
And I remember going to my
husband that night saying

00:17:03.255 --> 00:17:05.858 align:start position:0%
if I can't even get legislative
votes on the record,

00:17:05.858 --> 00:17:07.459
what am I doing here?

00:17:07.459 --> 00:17:09.294
And he said, then fight.

00:17:09.294 --> 00:17:12.164
So I went around the
state of South Carolina

00:17:12.164 --> 00:17:14.867
and said did you know of all
the bills passed in the house

00:17:14.867 --> 00:17:17.169
only 8% are on the record?

00:17:17.169 --> 00:17:19.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you know of all the
bills passed in the Senate

00:17:19.204 --> 00:17:21.473
only 1% was on the record?

00:17:21.473 --> 00:17:23.108
So if you did know
how your house member

00:17:23.108 --> 00:17:25.411
voted 92% of the time,

00:17:25.411 --> 00:17:28.514 align:start size:97% position:3%
if you didn't know how your
Senator voted 99% of the time,

00:17:28.514 --> 00:17:31.183
how did you know who to vote
for when you went to the polls?

00:17:31.183 --> 00:17:33.952 align:start size:84% position:16%
The people of South
Carolina were shocked.

00:17:33.952 --> 00:17:35.721
Now to put this
into perspective,

00:17:35.721 --> 00:17:36.955
my first Junior office,

00:17:36.955 --> 00:17:38.724
I was chairman of
the freshmen class,

00:17:38.724 --> 00:17:40.793
my second year I
was majority whip,

00:17:40.793 --> 00:17:42.928 align:start size:97% position:3%
my third year I was on a
powerful business committee,

00:17:42.928 --> 00:17:45.597 align:start size:97% position:3%
My fourth year I was
subcommittee chair of banking.

00:17:45.597 --> 00:17:47.699 align:start size:84% position:16%
The year that I didn't
put the bill away

00:17:47.699 --> 00:17:49.935
they stripped me of everything.

00:17:49.935 --> 00:17:51.503
I was completely blackballed,

00:17:51.503 --> 00:17:54.006
I could take the well,
no one would listen.

00:17:54.006 --> 00:17:57.609
I could sponsor a bill,
no one would co-sponsor.

00:17:57.609 --> 00:17:58.710
So I ran for governor.

00:17:59.845 --> 00:18:02.514 align:start size:88% position:13%
And one of the first
bills we signed into law

00:18:02.514 --> 00:18:04.149
is now in South Carolina.

00:18:04.149 --> 00:18:05.918
Everything debated
on for in the house

00:18:05.918 --> 00:18:07.820 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the Senate has to
have a vote on the record

00:18:07.820 --> 00:18:09.088
and we took it a step further

00:18:09.088 --> 00:18:11.723
and did every section
of the budget as well.

00:18:11.723 --> 00:18:14.760 align:start size:97% position:3%
- And you had a pretty solid
record in South Carolina.

00:18:14.760 --> 00:18:15.828 align:start size:84% position:16%
You're pretty proud
of that record.

00:18:15.828 --> 00:18:17.096
- Yes, very proud.

00:18:17.096 --> 00:18:21.467
I mean, we went from a
13% unemployment rate

00:18:21.467 --> 00:18:25.170 align:start position:0%
to the fact that South Carolina
didn't have any industry.

00:18:25.170 --> 00:18:27.639
All our jobs were in
the textile market

00:18:27.639 --> 00:18:29.174
and they had all gone overseas

00:18:29.174 --> 00:18:31.376
and we had to wake
South Carolina up.

00:18:31.376 --> 00:18:33.212
And so I went in there and said,

00:18:33.212 --> 00:18:34.947 align:start size:88% position:13%
if you're costing a
person or business time,

00:18:34.947 --> 00:18:36.381
you're costing them money,

00:18:36.381 --> 00:18:38.684 align:start size:97% position:3%
that's no longer acceptable
in South Carolina

00:18:38.684 --> 00:18:40.152
and we got to work.

00:18:40.152 --> 00:18:42.454
And by the time I left, we were
building planes with Boeing,

00:18:42.454 --> 00:18:45.691
more BMWs in any
place in the world,

00:18:45.691 --> 00:18:47.759 align:start size:81% position:19%
five international
tire companies,

00:18:47.759 --> 00:18:50.796
the largest carbon fiber
producer in the world.

00:18:50.796 --> 00:18:53.632
They were referring to us as
the beast of the Southeast

00:18:53.632 --> 00:18:54.800
and I loved it.

00:18:54.800 --> 00:18:56.034
And no unions.

00:18:56.034 --> 00:18:58.070 align:start size:84% position:16%
I was a union buster
the whole time,

00:18:58.070 --> 00:19:00.172
if there was a company
that wanted to come in

00:19:00.172 --> 00:19:02.307
that was unionized,
we strong-armed them

00:19:02.307 --> 00:19:03.876
and said we don't want you.

00:19:03.876 --> 00:19:05.344
- So what would you say

00:19:05.344 --> 00:19:07.412 align:start size:84% position:16%
your guiding political
principles are?

00:19:07.412 --> 00:19:08.680
Because it's interesting to me

00:19:08.680 --> 00:19:11.650
like you're 13 years
old doing the books,

00:19:11.650 --> 00:19:14.019
so like there's numbers
and those things matter,

00:19:14.019 --> 00:19:16.155 align:start size:97% position:3%
and now we live in this
bizarre time where everyone's

00:19:16.155 --> 00:19:19.358 align:start size:97% position:3%
like 2 trillion for this
and I just saw this morning,

00:19:19.358 --> 00:19:24.363
they want to pass another 80
billion to fortify the IRS.

00:19:24.963 --> 00:19:26.231
Like what?

00:19:26.231 --> 00:19:27.666
Like this, does anyone
look at math anymore?

00:19:27.666 --> 00:19:29.234
Do calculators exists?

00:19:29.234 --> 00:19:30.903
Like what's going on here?

00:19:30.903 --> 00:19:34.173
But did you have a sort of
guiding political principle?

00:19:34.173 --> 00:19:35.707
Like when did that sort
of all come together?

00:19:35.707 --> 00:19:37.309
- I mean, I really think at 13,

00:19:37.309 --> 00:19:40.212 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean I learned the
value of a dollar

00:19:40.212 --> 00:19:41.513
and I learned that that dollar

00:19:41.513 --> 00:19:43.148
you can only stretch it so far.

00:19:43.148 --> 00:19:46.752 align:start size:97% position:3%
And so really understanding
the value of a dollar,

00:19:46.752 --> 00:19:49.521 align:start size:84% position:16%
appreciating small
and limited government

00:19:49.521 --> 00:19:51.256
so that people can be successful

00:19:51.256 --> 00:19:53.225
without government
getting in the way,

00:19:53.225 --> 00:19:55.994 align:start size:97% position:3%
understanding the importance
of a good education

00:19:55.994 --> 00:20:00.199
and that education not being
government responding to money,

00:20:00.199 --> 00:20:02.434 align:start size:88% position:13%
but government actually
responding to kids

00:20:02.434 --> 00:20:05.237
and allowing families to
decide their education

00:20:05.237 --> 00:20:08.340 align:start size:97% position:3%
and then allowing job creators
to do what they do best

00:20:08.340 --> 00:20:09.741
which is create jobs.

00:20:11.109 --> 00:20:13.345
If small business makes money,

00:20:13.345 --> 00:20:16.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
they don't go on vacation,
they hire more people.

00:20:16.415 --> 00:20:18.884
And so the goal is you
want small businesses

00:20:18.884 --> 00:20:20.352
to have cash flow

00:20:20.352 --> 00:20:22.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
so they can spread the
tentacles out and do that.

00:20:22.921 --> 00:20:24.556
You want a strong foreign policy

00:20:24.556 --> 00:20:27.326 align:start size:88% position:13%
where you're making sure
you're safe overseas

00:20:27.326 --> 00:20:28.794
and it's not coming here.

00:20:28.794 --> 00:20:32.331 align:start size:97% position:3%
These are basic principles,
it's not rocket science

00:20:32.331 --> 00:20:35.367
but it's core values that
I think are at the heart

00:20:35.367 --> 00:20:36.868
of the Republican party,

00:20:36.868 --> 00:20:39.004 align:start size:88% position:13%
but they're at the heart
of a good America too

00:20:39.004 --> 00:20:40.539
if we do it right.

00:20:40.539 --> 00:20:42.441
- Yeah. So what was it like
the day you got the call,

00:20:42.441 --> 00:20:43.675 align:start size:84% position:16%
let's flash forward
a little bit,

00:20:43.675 --> 00:20:44.943
the day you get the call,

00:20:44.943 --> 00:20:47.179 align:start size:88% position:13%
would you like to be the
ambassador to the UN?

00:20:47.179 --> 00:20:48.447
I can only imagine

00:20:48.447 --> 00:20:50.015 align:start size:84% position:16%
because there's a
very legion of doom,

00:20:50.015 --> 00:20:52.584 line:0%
scary feeling over at the union.

00:20:52.584 --> 00:20:54.519 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
- The thing people don't
know is Donald Trump

00:20:54.519 --> 00:20:56.388 line:0%
and I knew each other before,

00:20:57.856 --> 00:21:01.593
when I won the primary for
governor the first time.

00:21:01.593 --> 00:21:04.329 align:start size:88% position:13%
I got this envelope with
this great gold trim

00:21:04.329 --> 00:21:06.198
and it was a support check,

00:21:06.198 --> 00:21:08.000
and there was a note that
said, you're a winner.

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:10.469
And so I got on the
phone and we chatted

00:21:10.469 --> 00:21:13.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we we're acquaintances
throughout the years

00:21:14.439 --> 00:21:16.742
and then 2016 happened.

00:21:16.742 --> 00:21:21.413
And we had a great slate
of talent on that stage,

00:21:21.413 --> 00:21:24.616
I put my name behind
a different horse.

00:21:24.616 --> 00:21:25.751
- Wait, who'd you
back originally?

00:21:25.751 --> 00:21:26.952
- Rubio.

00:21:26.952 --> 00:21:29.454 align:start size:84% position:16%
And then that's
when Trump tweeted,

00:21:29.454 --> 00:21:32.257 align:start size:97% position:3%
Nikki Haley's embarrassment
to South Carolina,

00:21:32.257 --> 00:21:35.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I turned around and
tweeted, bless your heart.

00:21:35.694 --> 00:21:37.696 align:start size:81% position:19%
We always had a
great respect for,

00:21:37.696 --> 00:21:39.531
I knew if you kicked
him, he kick back.

00:21:39.531 --> 00:21:41.733 align:start size:84% position:16%
He knew if you punched
me, I punch back.

00:21:41.733 --> 00:21:43.669
And so there was
a respect there.

00:21:43.669 --> 00:21:45.103
But after the primary,

00:21:45.103 --> 00:21:47.939
I threw all my support
behind him and he won.

00:21:47.939 --> 00:21:51.076 align:start size:97% position:3%
So when we got the call,
Reince Priebus said he wants

00:21:51.076 --> 00:21:52.311
to talk to you about...

00:21:54.446 --> 00:21:55.681
He said, don't say anything,

00:21:55.681 --> 00:21:57.816
US ambassador to
the United nations.

00:21:57.816 --> 00:21:59.084
I said Reince,

00:21:59.084 --> 00:22:00.052
I don't even know what
the United Nations does,

00:22:00.052 --> 00:22:02.054
I just know everybody hates it.

00:22:02.054 --> 00:22:03.655
And so he said, well,
he's going to call you.

00:22:03.655 --> 00:22:05.991 align:start size:88% position:13%
So when he called me,
he said, all right Nick,

00:22:05.991 --> 00:22:07.426
are you going to do this?

00:22:07.426 --> 00:22:10.162 align:start position:0%
And I said, well, I said,
there'd have to be some changes.

00:22:10.162 --> 00:22:11.363
And he said, what?

00:22:11.363 --> 00:22:12.631 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I said, well,
I've been a governor,

00:22:12.631 --> 00:22:14.599 align:start size:84% position:16%
I don't want to work
for anyone else,

00:22:14.599 --> 00:22:16.001 align:start size:84% position:16%
I would want to work
directly with you

00:22:16.001 --> 00:22:18.003
so I'd want to be
a cabinet member.

00:22:18.003 --> 00:22:19.271
He said done.

00:22:19.271 --> 00:22:20.739
I said, well, I'm a policy girl,

00:22:20.739 --> 00:22:22.841 align:start size:97% position:3%
So I'd want to be in the
room when decisions are made.

00:22:22.841 --> 00:22:25.210
so I'd want to be on the
National Security Council.

00:22:25.210 --> 00:22:26.678
He said done.

00:22:26.678 --> 00:22:28.113
I said well,

00:22:28.113 --> 00:22:29.348 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'm not going to be a
wallflower or talking head,

00:22:29.348 --> 00:22:30.882 align:start size:84% position:16%
I need to be able
to say what I think.

00:22:30.882 --> 00:22:32.117
And he said, Nikki

00:22:32.117 --> 00:22:33.652
that's exactly what I
want you to do this.

00:22:33.652 --> 00:22:34.886
And he was true to his word

00:22:34.886 --> 00:22:36.321
from the first day
to the last day.

00:22:36.321 --> 00:22:38.156 align:start size:84% position:16%
We had a great
working relationship.

00:22:38.156 --> 00:22:40.425
- So what was it like
going into the UN?

00:22:40.425 --> 00:22:41.927
Because I think you just
described it perfectly.

00:22:41.927 --> 00:22:43.862
I mean, it seems like
the most backwards,

00:22:43.862 --> 00:22:45.197 align:start size:84% position:16%
at least the security
council stuff,

00:22:45.197 --> 00:22:46.431
I know they do some...

00:22:46.431 --> 00:22:48.533
I suppose they do some
good humanitarian stuff.

00:22:48.533 --> 00:22:50.235
Maybe you can comment.

00:22:50.235 --> 00:22:52.070 align:start size:84% position:16%
Well, you can comment
on that obviously

00:22:52.070 --> 00:22:53.372
but like to just go in there

00:22:53.372 --> 00:22:56.041 align:start size:84% position:16%
and try to at least
defend freedom,

00:22:56.041 --> 00:22:58.910
try to get some of
these insane votes

00:22:58.910 --> 00:23:00.579 align:start size:88% position:13%
that they're constantly
doing reversed

00:23:00.579 --> 00:23:02.114
and change some of that stuff.

00:23:02.114 --> 00:23:03.648
Like I'm guessing you were
walking down the hallway.

00:23:03.648 --> 00:23:06.118
People were not like, oh,
yay, there's Nikki Haley.

00:23:07.319 --> 00:23:09.654
- The UN is not for
the faint of heart.

00:23:09.654 --> 00:23:11.857
I mean, every day it
felt like I was putting

00:23:11.857 --> 00:23:14.393
on body armor and you
knew we'd have a fight,

00:23:14.393 --> 00:23:16.795 align:start position:0%
you just didn't know which
country we're fighting that day.

00:23:16.795 --> 00:23:20.232 align:start position:0%
But how blessed was I to defend
the country I love so much.

00:23:20.232 --> 00:23:23.902
And I was not going to let them
criticize us about anything.

00:23:23.902 --> 00:23:27.572 align:start size:97% position:3%
I purposely went in not
knowing the do's and don'ts

00:23:27.572 --> 00:23:30.642
of the UN, because I wanted
to kind of be able to ask

00:23:30.642 --> 00:23:34.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
for forgiveness and really
go in with fresh eyes.

00:23:34.513 --> 00:23:37.082
But I also knew I wanted
to be very black and white.

00:23:37.082 --> 00:23:38.617
I wanted to make sure they knew

00:23:38.617 --> 00:23:40.719
what United States was for
and what we were against.

00:23:40.719 --> 00:23:42.020
And there was no gray area.

00:23:42.020 --> 00:23:43.722
I didn't care if they liked me

00:23:43.722 --> 00:23:45.857
but I wanted them to America.

00:23:45.857 --> 00:23:47.559
And I wanted them to
know where we stood.

00:23:47.559 --> 00:23:51.229 align:start size:88% position:13%
Obama had really created
this scenario where

00:23:51.229 --> 00:23:53.632
they didn't know
what we were for.

00:23:53.632 --> 00:23:56.601 align:start position:0%
When he tried to appease
everybody by criticizing the US

00:23:56.601 --> 00:23:58.270 align:start size:84% position:16%
and he would just
throw foreign aid out

00:23:58.270 --> 00:24:00.238
to everyone to buy friends.

00:24:00.238 --> 00:24:01.740
I didn't want any of that.

00:24:01.740 --> 00:24:04.309
I wanted to make sure that
we really put our line down

00:24:04.309 --> 00:24:06.378
in the sand of this
is where we are.

00:24:06.378 --> 00:24:08.980
If you want to join us,
we will partner with you

00:24:08.980 --> 00:24:11.082 align:start size:97% position:3%
and if you don't, we're
going to call you out for it.

00:24:11.082 --> 00:24:13.885
And so that's why I said we
were taking names at the UN.

00:24:13.885 --> 00:24:16.221 align:start size:84% position:16%
They thought that
was like unbelievable

00:24:16.221 --> 00:24:18.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I would say
something so undiplomatic.

00:24:18.857 --> 00:24:22.794
But the point was, if you go
around saying death to America,

00:24:22.794 --> 00:24:24.296
we're going to take down names.

00:24:24.296 --> 00:24:25.897
But if you're our
friend and ally,

00:24:25.897 --> 00:24:27.899
we're going to have your
back and take down names

00:24:27.899 --> 00:24:29.167
and protect you too.

00:24:29.167 --> 00:24:32.504
And so look, it was
a great experience,

00:24:32.504 --> 00:24:34.506
it's challenging to
deal with the Chinese

00:24:34.506 --> 00:24:36.808 align:start size:97% position:3%
and to have the Russians
always trying to stir the pot

00:24:36.808 --> 00:24:40.045
and to have everybody talk
negatively about America.

00:24:40.045 --> 00:24:41.413
But I wasn't going
to stand for it.

00:24:41.413 --> 00:24:43.014
I went and take one second of it

00:24:43.014 --> 00:24:46.251
because I know how great we are.

00:24:46.251 --> 00:24:47.819 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I knew what
they were telling me

00:24:47.819 --> 00:24:49.654
in the quarters of
how great we were.

00:24:49.654 --> 00:24:51.156 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Yeah. So that that's
actually exactly

00:24:51.156 --> 00:24:52.657
what I wanted to ask you.

00:24:52.657 --> 00:24:55.327
So like, I would imagine that
the country secretly believe

00:24:55.327 --> 00:24:56.695
that most of the countries.

00:24:56.695 --> 00:24:58.263
Like they secretly must be like

00:24:58.263 --> 00:25:00.732 align:start size:84% position:16%
yeah, the us doesn't
exist in freedom,

00:25:00.732 --> 00:25:02.534
then we're all kind of screwed,

00:25:02.534 --> 00:25:04.569 align:start size:84% position:16%
but then they
rarely vote that way

00:25:04.569 --> 00:25:06.304
or publicly they say all
these ridiculous things.

00:25:06.304 --> 00:25:07.806
- No. They bash us publicly

00:25:07.806 --> 00:25:10.909
but what they would say
is they wanted us to lead

00:25:10.909 --> 00:25:12.477 align:start size:84% position:16%
because they don't
want to follow Russia,

00:25:12.477 --> 00:25:14.079
they don't want to
wanna follow China,

00:25:14.079 --> 00:25:17.015
they do see us as the
moral authority there.

00:25:17.015 --> 00:25:18.550 align:start size:84% position:16%
And you know it
was perfect example

00:25:18.550 --> 00:25:23.388
is when Syria crossed the red
line and did chemical weapons,

00:25:24.789 --> 00:25:28.693 align:start size:97% position:3%
and Trump did the first shots
back and did the missiles

00:25:28.693 --> 00:25:30.829 align:start size:94% position:6%
the number of ambassadors
that came to me

00:25:30.829 --> 00:25:33.899
and said it's so good to see
the United States lead again.

00:25:33.899 --> 00:25:36.268
Like that's what they want.

00:25:36.268 --> 00:25:38.136
They want us to call out evil,

00:25:38.136 --> 00:25:41.406 align:start size:97% position:3%
they want us to do good, they
want us to show something

00:25:41.406 --> 00:25:43.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that's why I've always
said the United States

00:25:43.642 --> 00:25:45.911
leadership isn't going to war.

00:25:45.911 --> 00:25:48.680
Sometimes just when
the United States

00:25:48.680 --> 00:25:51.583
says something,
countries follow.

00:25:51.583 --> 00:25:54.119
When we mentioned this
is what should happen,

00:25:54.119 --> 00:25:56.321
they do tend to move with us.

00:25:56.321 --> 00:25:58.323
And so there's good
that we have there

00:25:58.323 --> 00:26:00.725 align:start size:88% position:13%
but we have to continue
to use that voice

00:26:00.725 --> 00:26:01.960
and be a force for good.

00:26:01.960 --> 00:26:04.062 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Can you explain
either your philosophy

00:26:04.062 --> 00:26:05.997
or Trump's philosophy or
both of your philosophies,

00:26:05.997 --> 00:26:09.167
just generally on when you
should use the military?

00:26:09.167 --> 00:26:11.570
Because I think a lot
of people think somehow

00:26:11.570 --> 00:26:13.171
if you're for the military,

00:26:13.171 --> 00:26:14.372 align:start size:97% position:3%
that means you were for war
and it's actually the reverse.

00:26:14.372 --> 00:26:16.741
- And that's not
the case at all.

00:26:16.741 --> 00:26:20.612
I mean, the key is look,
I'm in a military family,

00:26:20.612 --> 00:26:22.147
so the last thing
I'm going to say

00:26:22.147 --> 00:26:26.117 align:start position:0%
is with my brother was full-time
military, my husband is,

00:26:26.117 --> 00:26:28.653
the last thing you want your
family members to go to war.

00:26:28.653 --> 00:26:31.022
But the military is
there for a reason.

00:26:31.022 --> 00:26:34.225 align:start size:84% position:16%
And what you do
want is for example,

00:26:35.727 --> 00:26:38.196 align:start size:88% position:13%
with Biden wanting to
pull out of Afghanistan.

00:26:38.196 --> 00:26:40.465 align:start size:84% position:16%
Well, my husband
served in Afghanistan,

00:26:40.465 --> 00:26:41.666
I know what was happening there,

00:26:41.666 --> 00:26:44.002 align:start size:88% position:13%
we don't need thousands
of troops there

00:26:44.002 --> 00:26:47.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you do need some
there for intel purposes.

00:26:47.105 --> 00:26:50.375
That's really what you want
is military for intelligence,

00:26:50.375 --> 00:26:52.410 align:start size:81% position:19%
to tell you on the
ground in Syria

00:26:52.410 --> 00:26:53.445
whether they're getting ready

00:26:53.445 --> 00:26:54.879
to do a chemical weapons attack,

00:26:54.879 --> 00:26:56.982
to tell you on the
ground in Afghanistan

00:26:56.982 --> 00:26:59.551 align:start size:84% position:16%
whether there's
another plot for 911.

00:26:59.551 --> 00:27:03.655
So the only thing I'll say is
that Biden's Foreign Policy

00:27:03.655 --> 00:27:07.726
is really backwards in the
way that look at how much

00:27:07.726 --> 00:27:10.895
has changed from the Chinese
delegation comes to Alaska

00:27:10.895 --> 00:27:13.064
and humiliates our
American delegation.

00:27:13.064 --> 00:27:15.433
Putin's challenging
Biden to a debate,

00:27:15.433 --> 00:27:17.369
how ridiculous is that?

00:27:17.369 --> 00:27:20.105 align:start size:97% position:3%
Chema is starting to test
off ballistic missiles again,

00:27:20.105 --> 00:27:22.474 align:start size:88% position:13%
and here Biden's
falling all over himself

00:27:22.474 --> 00:27:25.744
to do business with Iran
but is boycotting Georgia?

00:27:25.744 --> 00:27:28.179
Like these things and
then all of that--

00:27:28.179 --> 00:27:29.681
- Georgia the state not
Georgia the country.

00:27:29.681 --> 00:27:31.216
- Absolutely.

00:27:31.216 --> 00:27:33.685
And all these things and he's
cutting our defense spending.

00:27:33.685 --> 00:27:36.087 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'll be the first one to
say the military is bloated,

00:27:36.087 --> 00:27:37.455
it's bureaucratic,

00:27:37.455 --> 00:27:39.524 align:start size:88% position:13%
there's a lot that we
shouldn't be paying for,

00:27:39.524 --> 00:27:42.560 align:start size:88% position:13%
but if we don't
modernize our military,

00:27:42.560 --> 00:27:44.562
China and Russia already moving,

00:27:44.562 --> 00:27:46.131
Iran is already speeding up,

00:27:46.131 --> 00:27:48.700
we look so distracted right now.

00:27:48.700 --> 00:27:52.003 align:start size:88% position:13%
And making sure we
modernize our military,

00:27:52.003 --> 00:27:54.673 align:start size:97% position:3%
making sure we have strategic
military on the ground

00:27:54.673 --> 00:27:57.075
in certain places
to keep us safe

00:27:57.075 --> 00:27:59.411
and to keep bad actors
from doing more harm,

00:27:59.411 --> 00:28:00.912
that's an important thing.

00:28:00.912 --> 00:28:03.615 align:start size:84% position:16%
- So what do you
think is behind Biden

00:28:03.615 --> 00:28:05.316
and the decisions he's making?

00:28:05.316 --> 00:28:07.118
This is the question
that everyone gets
asked all the time.

00:28:07.118 --> 00:28:09.621
Like, because I think most
people don't really believe

00:28:09.621 --> 00:28:11.623
it's Biden leading
this thing anymore,

00:28:11.623 --> 00:28:14.259
that it's either the
Obama machine behind it

00:28:14.259 --> 00:28:16.227
or something that's left
of the Clinton machine

00:28:16.227 --> 00:28:17.762
or something else altogether.

00:28:17.762 --> 00:28:20.031
Like, to me it seems like if
you would've asked Joe Biden

00:28:20.031 --> 00:28:22.033
10 years ago, if he
agreed or disagreed

00:28:22.033 --> 00:28:23.468
with some of the things
you just said there,

00:28:23.468 --> 00:28:26.004 align:start size:97% position:3%
he probably would have
agreed where now it's like,

00:28:26.004 --> 00:28:27.238
who knows what he believes.

00:28:27.238 --> 00:28:29.507
- What it feels
like to me coming

00:28:29.507 --> 00:28:31.943
in the transition from Obama

00:28:31.943 --> 00:28:33.978 align:start size:97% position:3%
to the Trump administration
and Foreign Policy

00:28:33.978 --> 00:28:35.180
and now where it's going,

00:28:35.180 --> 00:28:37.816 align:start size:84% position:16%
it really does feel
like Obama 2.0.

00:28:37.816 --> 00:28:39.884
I mean the idea that they're
already trying to make friends

00:28:39.884 --> 00:28:43.188 align:start size:97% position:3%
with Iran that was very much
something Obama would do.

00:28:43.188 --> 00:28:46.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
The idea that they're like
starting to pick fights

00:28:46.658 --> 00:28:49.160
with Russia in a
strong man sense

00:28:49.160 --> 00:28:51.062
but not in real results sense,

00:28:51.062 --> 00:28:52.964
that's something Obama would do.

00:28:52.964 --> 00:28:55.266 align:start size:97% position:3%
The Paris Climate Agreement,
the Human Rights Council,

00:28:55.266 --> 00:28:56.768
all these things,

00:28:56.768 --> 00:28:59.604
these Trump reversals are
very much Obama stances.

00:28:59.604 --> 00:29:03.575
And so I think that that's
the approach Biden's taken.

00:29:03.575 --> 00:29:06.277 align:start size:84% position:16%
He surrounded himself
by Obama people,

00:29:06.277 --> 00:29:08.379
whether it's secretary Blinken

00:29:08.379 --> 00:29:09.914
or Jake Sullivan
or any of those,

00:29:09.914 --> 00:29:13.017
those are all Obama people
that would be advising him

00:29:13.017 --> 00:29:14.686
on what Obama wants.

00:29:14.686 --> 00:29:17.856
- So what can be done at
the international level

00:29:17.856 --> 00:29:19.424
like with the UN at this point?

00:29:19.424 --> 00:29:21.092
Like if you were
there right now,

00:29:21.092 --> 00:29:22.260 align:start size:84% position:16%
which probably ain't
going to happen,

00:29:22.260 --> 00:29:24.062
but if you were there right now,

00:29:24.062 --> 00:29:25.630 align:start size:88% position:13%
I mean, this just in
the last couple of days,

00:29:25.630 --> 00:29:29.567
Iran got put on the, was it
the Women's Rights Council?

00:29:29.567 --> 00:29:30.802
- The Women's Council.

00:29:30.802 --> 00:29:33.671
I mean, how ridiculous is that?

00:29:33.671 --> 00:29:34.906
- Like all these people
are laughing a bit but--

00:29:34.906 --> 00:29:36.508 align:start size:88% position:13%
- And it was not only
Iran, it was also China.

00:29:36.508 --> 00:29:38.343
This is like an absurd.

00:29:38.343 --> 00:29:39.577
- But who makes these decisions?

00:29:39.577 --> 00:29:41.412
Like someone goes into meeting

00:29:41.412 --> 00:29:42.614
and they're like, yes, yes,

00:29:42.614 --> 00:29:44.749
let's put her on the
Women's Rights Council.

00:29:44.749 --> 00:29:46.718
Like how does that even happen?

00:29:46.718 --> 00:29:49.420 align:start size:97% position:3%
- It's why the United Nations
doesn't have credibility,

00:29:49.420 --> 00:29:50.889
it's why they struggle.

00:29:50.889 --> 00:29:52.991 align:start size:97% position:3%
First of all, if I was at
the United Nations right now,

00:29:52.991 --> 00:29:55.226
I would immediately call
a security council hearing

00:29:55.226 --> 00:29:57.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
and hold China accountable
for what they did

00:29:57.262 --> 00:29:58.797
to the world with COVID.

00:29:58.797 --> 00:30:01.132
I would ask what the World
Health Organization knew.

00:30:01.132 --> 00:30:04.035 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would call out Iran
for all of the violations

00:30:04.035 --> 00:30:06.638
of UN resolutions
that they're doing

00:30:06.638 --> 00:30:09.207 align:start position:0%
and say how can you turn around
and get into an Iran deal

00:30:09.207 --> 00:30:12.110
when they're violating
multiple resolutions.

00:30:12.110 --> 00:30:14.312 align:start size:88% position:13%
There's a lot of things
that could be done

00:30:14.312 --> 00:30:15.814
and should be done,

00:30:15.814 --> 00:30:17.916
and instead what we've seen
is the UN ambassador went

00:30:17.916 --> 00:30:20.451 align:start size:84% position:16%
and basically
criticized America.

00:30:20.451 --> 00:30:23.054
- Was there any speech that you
had heard in the last couple

00:30:23.054 --> 00:30:24.989
of years that were just
more awful than that?

00:30:24.989 --> 00:30:26.424
- Modified.

00:30:26.424 --> 00:30:29.761
That here I was
defending America

00:30:29.761 --> 00:30:33.097 align:start size:84% position:16%
and here the Chinese
delegation goes

00:30:33.097 --> 00:30:35.733
and humiliates the
American delegation

00:30:35.733 --> 00:30:38.102
and the UN ambassador
basically gave them

00:30:38.102 --> 00:30:39.370
all the fuel to do it.

00:30:40.939 --> 00:30:42.574
We are not a racist country,

00:30:42.574 --> 00:30:44.342
we are the least racist country.

00:30:44.342 --> 00:30:48.713 align:start size:97% position:3%
And so the idea that they
would say that it's such a...

00:30:48.713 --> 00:30:51.282 align:start size:84% position:16%
I can't even
understand what Biden

00:30:51.282 --> 00:30:54.752 align:start size:97% position:3%
or the ambassador think that
will do to help America.

00:30:54.752 --> 00:30:56.955
That's apologizing for America.

00:30:56.955 --> 00:30:58.256
- I don't think they want to
help America at this point.

00:30:58.256 --> 00:30:59.991
That's what I mean about Biden,

00:30:59.991 --> 00:31:01.426
I don't know what Biden believes

00:31:01.426 --> 00:31:03.728 align:start size:97% position:3%
but I think the machine
that's under him or behind him

00:31:03.728 --> 00:31:05.763
or whatever it is like, do
they want to help America?

00:31:05.763 --> 00:31:07.298
- It was so embarrassing.

00:31:07.298 --> 00:31:08.499
It made me sad.

00:31:08.499 --> 00:31:11.002 align:start size:88% position:13%
I mean, you talked about
what can the UN do?

00:31:11.002 --> 00:31:12.403
What is it good for?

00:31:12.403 --> 00:31:15.707 align:start size:97% position:3%
The reason presidents struggle
with staying in the UN

00:31:15.707 --> 00:31:19.978 align:start size:88% position:13%
is not because of any
great actions by the UN,

00:31:19.978 --> 00:31:21.679
we see that all the time.

00:31:21.679 --> 00:31:24.515 align:start size:97% position:3%
I think the reason they
stay is because of the veto.

00:31:24.515 --> 00:31:26.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
There are only five
countries that have a veto

00:31:26.451 --> 00:31:31.356 align:start size:97% position:3%
on the security council in
the UN, Russia, China, US, UK,

00:31:31.356 --> 00:31:33.424
who am I missing, France.

00:31:34.592 --> 00:31:38.529 align:start size:88% position:13%
So if you look at those,
if bad things happen,

00:31:38.529 --> 00:31:40.832
if Russia and China
try and get together

00:31:40.832 --> 00:31:43.434
and do something bad,
the US can stop it.

00:31:43.434 --> 00:31:46.704 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
That's the reason that we're
on the security council

00:31:46.704 --> 00:31:49.140 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
is we can stop bad
things from happening.

00:31:49.140 --> 00:31:51.476 align:start size:88% position:13%
But they waste more
than they should ever...

00:31:51.476 --> 00:31:55.013
I cut $3 billion the first
year off of that budget.

00:31:55.013 --> 00:31:56.314
And that was just low hanging.

00:31:56.314 --> 00:31:57.515
- And the lights didn't go out.

00:31:57.515 --> 00:31:58.983
The building still existed.

00:31:58.983 --> 00:32:00.418
- And people see
that big building

00:32:00.418 --> 00:32:01.819
and they think they're
ambassadors in there,

00:32:01.819 --> 00:32:03.488
that's all staff.

00:32:03.488 --> 00:32:06.291
They've got elevator
operators in there.

00:32:06.291 --> 00:32:08.293 align:start size:84% position:16%
I would say, do you
know how many vaccines

00:32:08.293 --> 00:32:09.861 align:start size:88% position:13%
you could give kids
with what you're paying

00:32:09.861 --> 00:32:11.396
these elevator operators?

00:32:11.396 --> 00:32:13.798 align:start size:88% position:13%
They doubled their staff
in the last 10 years.

00:32:13.798 --> 00:32:15.033
- And don't they...

00:32:15.033 --> 00:32:16.301
Wasn't there some
massive scandal

00:32:16.301 --> 00:32:17.735
where they were like
racking up something

00:32:17.735 --> 00:32:19.938 align:start size:97% position:3%
like a hundred million dollars
worth of parking tickets

00:32:19.938 --> 00:32:20.872
in New York city?

00:32:20.872 --> 00:32:21.673
Like it's just crazy over there.

00:32:21.673 --> 00:32:22.907
- It's so ridiculous.

00:32:22.907 --> 00:32:25.243 align:start size:84% position:16%
China is infiltrating
the entire UN.

00:32:25.243 --> 00:32:26.744
They are trying to really,

00:32:26.744 --> 00:32:29.714
I think they now control
four different agencies

00:32:29.714 --> 00:32:34.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
within the UN, Russia
controls the cyber agency,

00:32:34.519 --> 00:32:35.954
believe it or not.

00:32:35.954 --> 00:32:38.990 align:start position:0%
China almost started controlling
the intellectual property

00:32:38.990 --> 00:32:40.992 align:start size:88% position:13%
and we were able to stop
that from happening.

00:32:40.992 --> 00:32:44.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I mean, it's just, the
UN will not be relevant

00:32:44.228 --> 00:32:45.863 align:start size:88% position:13%
until they start
talking about the things

00:32:45.863 --> 00:32:47.432 align:start size:84% position:16%
that are uncomfortable
to talk about.

00:32:47.432 --> 00:32:50.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
The Uyghur genocide
that's happening in China,

00:32:50.101 --> 00:32:51.369
the fact that--

00:32:51.369 --> 00:32:52.437 align:start size:84% position:16%
- They won't even have
a meeting about it.

00:32:52.437 --> 00:32:54.138
- They won't even do it.

00:32:54.138 --> 00:32:55.840
- So what do we do with China

00:32:55.840 --> 00:32:57.208
or what do we do with China?

00:32:58.443 --> 00:33:00.545
Like are we on some
inevitable collision

00:33:00.545 --> 00:33:01.746
no matter what here?

00:33:01.746 --> 00:33:03.214 align:start size:84% position:16%
Just because of debt
if nothing else,

00:33:03.214 --> 00:33:05.183
like if they just call in,

00:33:05.183 --> 00:33:06.684 align:start size:97% position:3%
hey guys you gotta pay us
back for some of this stuff.

00:33:06.684 --> 00:33:09.487
And then it's like, well, we
can't, we don't have the money.

00:33:09.487 --> 00:33:11.823 align:start size:84% position:16%
and we do have
missiles and bombs.

00:33:11.823 --> 00:33:14.892
- It's actually pretty scary
what's happening right now

00:33:14.892 --> 00:33:18.162
because China is our number
one foreign policy threat.

00:33:18.162 --> 00:33:20.932
But the concern
I have is America

00:33:20.932 --> 00:33:23.167
looks so distractive right now.

00:33:23.167 --> 00:33:26.604 align:start size:97% position:3%
Like everything, all these
countries see us as distracted

00:33:26.604 --> 00:33:30.008
but China is in this
for the long haul.

00:33:30.008 --> 00:33:33.444 align:start size:88% position:13%
And the US at some point
has to quit thinking

00:33:33.444 --> 00:33:35.913
about things in terms of
presidential elections.

00:33:35.913 --> 00:33:38.116 align:start size:97% position:3%
We've got to start thinking
20 and 30 years out,

00:33:38.116 --> 00:33:40.418 align:start size:84% position:16%
what does our foreign
policy look like?

00:33:40.418 --> 00:33:41.886
If you look at China,

00:33:41.886 --> 00:33:43.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
they have the largest
Naval fleet in the world,

00:33:43.254 --> 00:33:44.856 align:start size:88% position:13%
they have more missiles
than we do now,

00:33:44.856 --> 00:33:46.624
they're building
up their military,

00:33:46.624 --> 00:33:49.594
we've got to start
modernizing ours.

00:33:49.594 --> 00:33:51.863 align:start size:97% position:3%
They are continuing to
steal intellectual property,

00:33:51.863 --> 00:33:53.798 align:start size:88% position:13%
we've got to start
holding them accountable

00:33:53.798 --> 00:33:56.467
for every time they steal
that intellectual property.

00:33:56.467 --> 00:33:57.835
- What does that actually mean?

00:33:57.835 --> 00:33:59.771
Because what do we
have at this point

00:33:59.771 --> 00:34:01.472
beyond the threat
of military action.

00:34:01.472 --> 00:34:03.374 align:start size:84% position:16%
Like we're not bombing
China tomorrow.

00:34:04.509 --> 00:34:07.145 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Look, sanctions
and stopping business

00:34:07.145 --> 00:34:09.480
with China is a
big deal to them.

00:34:09.480 --> 00:34:12.417 align:start size:97% position:3%
Humiliating them and calling
them out is a big deal.

00:34:12.417 --> 00:34:14.419 align:start size:84% position:16%
They have a million
Muslim Uyghurs

00:34:14.419 --> 00:34:15.887
that are in concentration camps.

00:34:15.887 --> 00:34:18.489
If you saw what was
happening there,

00:34:18.489 --> 00:34:22.260 align:start size:88% position:13%
it's horrific, it's
rape, it's sexual abuse,

00:34:22.260 --> 00:34:25.263 align:start size:88% position:13%
it's physical abuse,
it's forced slave labor,

00:34:25.263 --> 00:34:27.298
I mean, making them
change their name,

00:34:27.298 --> 00:34:29.967
change their religion, drink
alcohol for the first time

00:34:29.967 --> 00:34:33.071
just to break them, I mean,
it's a horrible situation.

00:34:33.071 --> 00:34:37.208 align:start position:0%
We swore years ago, never again,
would we turn our eyes away

00:34:37.208 --> 00:34:39.544 align:start size:84% position:16%
from genocide and it's
happening right now

00:34:39.544 --> 00:34:41.379 align:start size:84% position:16%
and no one is calling
China out for it.

00:34:41.379 --> 00:34:42.814
It's the reason why
they get so important

00:34:42.814 --> 00:34:45.383
that we boycott the
Chinese Olympics,

00:34:45.383 --> 00:34:47.952
is because in the last Olympics,

00:34:47.952 --> 00:34:50.121
the way Beijing looked
at it was the last one

00:34:50.121 --> 00:34:52.657
that they hosted was
their coming out party.

00:34:52.657 --> 00:34:56.561
This one, mark, my words,
this one is them saying

00:34:56.561 --> 00:34:58.529 align:start size:88% position:13%
we are the new
superpower of the world.

00:34:58.529 --> 00:34:59.831
And after that Olympics

00:34:59.831 --> 00:35:02.066 align:start size:84% position:16%
they will go and
try and take Taiwan.

00:35:02.066 --> 00:35:03.835
And if they take Taiwan,

00:35:03.835 --> 00:35:06.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's a total game
changer around the world.

00:35:06.604 --> 00:35:09.907
And so they're trying to get
as much good press as they can.

00:35:09.907 --> 00:35:12.577 align:start size:84% position:16%
If we call them
out, they hate that.

00:35:12.577 --> 00:35:16.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
So making sure that we
call them out on genocide,

00:35:16.214 --> 00:35:19.684 align:start size:97% position:3%
making sure that we actually
hold them accountable

00:35:19.684 --> 00:35:20.852
on intellectual property,

00:35:20.852 --> 00:35:23.387 align:start size:88% position:13%
modernizing our military
which scares them

00:35:23.387 --> 00:35:26.757 align:start size:97% position:3%
or having a military presence
anywhere scares them.

00:35:26.757 --> 00:35:28.759
You go and you look at
what president Xi did,

00:35:28.759 --> 00:35:30.995 align:start size:88% position:13%
he started a commission
that basically

00:35:30.995 --> 00:35:33.731 align:start size:88% position:13%
said any company that
does business with China

00:35:33.731 --> 00:35:36.767
has to cooperate with
our Chinese military.

00:35:36.767 --> 00:35:39.070 align:start size:84% position:16%
Now think about
our tech companies,

00:35:39.070 --> 00:35:41.839 align:start position:0%
think about all the information
they have on our habits,

00:35:41.839 --> 00:35:44.509 align:start size:88% position:13%
on our pharmaceuticals,
on everything we do

00:35:44.509 --> 00:35:47.445 align:start size:97% position:3%
and now know the Chinese
military has access to that.

00:35:47.445 --> 00:35:48.913
Think about that.

00:35:48.913 --> 00:35:51.816
Like that's dangerous and
we watch this play out

00:35:51.816 --> 00:35:53.618
in real time with COVID,

00:35:53.618 --> 00:35:56.854
that when we were trying
to save millions of lives

00:35:56.854 --> 00:35:58.022
what was China doing?

00:35:58.022 --> 00:35:59.590 align:start size:84% position:16%
They called to
American companies,

00:35:59.590 --> 00:36:02.193
3M and Honeywell who
have business in China,

00:36:02.193 --> 00:36:05.196
said you are not allowed
to sell any of your PPE.

00:36:05.196 --> 00:36:06.631
They'd bought it wholesale,

00:36:06.631 --> 00:36:08.566
and they would only
give it to countries

00:36:08.566 --> 00:36:12.003 align:start size:97% position:3%
that agreed to do business
with Huawei, their 5G network.

00:36:12.003 --> 00:36:15.106
This is a country that is out

00:36:15.106 --> 00:36:18.609
to really take over the
world and do all that.

00:36:18.609 --> 00:36:20.945 align:start position:0%
That's what all these
investments around the world are

00:36:20.945 --> 00:36:23.314 align:start size:84% position:16%
is when they're
running up this debt,

00:36:23.314 --> 00:36:25.283
then they go and they say
to these all countries,

00:36:25.283 --> 00:36:27.285
okay give us your
military and such,

00:36:27.285 --> 00:36:31.289
give us your utility and
the debt that we're in,

00:36:31.289 --> 00:36:34.192
is the first time our debt
is bigger than our economy

00:36:34.192 --> 00:36:35.159
since World War II.

00:36:35.159 --> 00:36:36.327
Do you know what that does?

00:36:36.327 --> 00:36:37.862
Makes China so happy

00:36:37.862 --> 00:36:40.565
because when you weaken
the dollar like that,

00:36:40.565 --> 00:36:43.501
that's a national security
threat beyond anything else.

00:36:43.501 --> 00:36:45.269
There's a reason China and Iran

00:36:45.269 --> 00:36:47.305
just got into a bank together

00:36:47.305 --> 00:36:49.774
is they're trying to make
sure that the US dollar

00:36:49.774 --> 00:36:51.242
is no longer the
world's reserve.

00:36:51.242 --> 00:36:54.645
And we're sitting back
and watching this happen

00:36:54.645 --> 00:36:56.881
and not doing anything about it.

00:36:56.881 --> 00:36:58.983
- So do you think no one in
the administration gets it?

00:36:58.983 --> 00:37:01.652
Because I think most people
watching this are probably,

00:37:01.652 --> 00:37:03.321
even if they're not that
in the weeds on all this,

00:37:03.321 --> 00:37:04.855 align:start size:84% position:16%
they're probably like,
yeah that does feel

00:37:04.855 --> 00:37:06.357
like basically what's happening.

00:37:06.357 --> 00:37:08.926 align:start size:97% position:3%
That China is saying we're
going to be the new superpower

00:37:08.926 --> 00:37:11.362
and they're setting up
all the pieces in play.

00:37:11.362 --> 00:37:12.530
But do you think anyone,

00:37:12.530 --> 00:37:14.065 align:start size:84% position:16%
do you think the
administration cares?

00:37:14.065 --> 00:37:17.034
- I think the US is
playing to symptoms.

00:37:17.034 --> 00:37:18.402
So they see what China's doing

00:37:18.402 --> 00:37:19.971 align:start size:84% position:16%
and they're treating
like symptoms

00:37:19.971 --> 00:37:22.273 align:start size:84% position:16%
but they're not
treating the disease.

00:37:22.273 --> 00:37:25.376 align:start size:97% position:3%
That China is a disease that
we have to stop thinking

00:37:25.376 --> 00:37:28.012
if we're nice to them,
which Kerry just said,

00:37:28.012 --> 00:37:29.480
oh, we should be nice with China

00:37:29.480 --> 00:37:31.649
so we can cooperate
on the environment.

00:37:32.850 --> 00:37:34.752
We have to stop thinking
if you're nice to China

00:37:34.752 --> 00:37:35.720
they'll want to be like us.

00:37:35.720 --> 00:37:36.988
They don't want to be like us.

00:37:36.988 --> 00:37:38.489
They want to be communist.

00:37:38.489 --> 00:37:40.157
They're going to continue
to do whatever it takes.

00:37:40.157 --> 00:37:41.959
They're laughing
at us right now.

00:37:41.959 --> 00:37:44.362
What we have to do is let
China know we're onto them

00:37:44.362 --> 00:37:46.230
and we have to act accordingly.

00:37:46.230 --> 00:37:50.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now that doesn't mean
that they can't buy grains

00:37:50.234 --> 00:37:51.736
and poultry from us,

00:37:51.736 --> 00:37:53.904
or we can't buy T-shirts
and light bulbs from them,

00:37:53.904 --> 00:37:55.406
but it does mean they don't get

00:37:55.406 --> 00:37:57.008
to control our pharmaceuticals.

00:37:57.008 --> 00:37:59.510
We don't need to go in so
much debt that they own us.

00:37:59.510 --> 00:38:01.912
Like there's certain things we
just need to be smart about,

00:38:01.912 --> 00:38:05.983 align:start position:0%
strategic about, instead of
just curing the little symptoms

00:38:05.983 --> 00:38:07.418
that come up along the way.

00:38:07.418 --> 00:38:08.919 align:start position:0%
- Do you think part of the
problem with some of this stuff

00:38:08.919 --> 00:38:10.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that now and I think
you were alluding to this,

00:38:10.454 --> 00:38:12.857 align:start size:97% position:3%
that now so much of our
conversation is about race,

00:38:12.857 --> 00:38:15.293 align:start position:0%
it's about all of this internal
stuff here and woke-ness

00:38:15.293 --> 00:38:16.661
and cancel culture and all this,

00:38:16.661 --> 00:38:19.363
but the idea of this big problem

00:38:19.363 --> 00:38:22.533
that like sits there people are
just like, oh, I don't know,

00:38:22.533 --> 00:38:24.468
we got enough problems here.

00:38:24.468 --> 00:38:25.736
Even though I think in many ways

00:38:25.736 --> 00:38:27.672
our problems here are
completely fabricated.

00:38:27.672 --> 00:38:28.939
- We do have big problems here

00:38:28.939 --> 00:38:30.941
and we do have big
problems overseas.

00:38:30.941 --> 00:38:32.977 align:start size:97% position:3%
We should be able to handle
both at the same time.

00:38:32.977 --> 00:38:34.278
Like it's not an
either or scenario.

00:38:34.278 --> 00:38:35.579
- You are saying we can
do two things at once?

00:38:35.579 --> 00:38:38.149 align:start size:84% position:16%
- I mean, there's
something to be said

00:38:38.149 --> 00:38:40.284
for balance and prioritizing

00:38:40.284 --> 00:38:43.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
and making sure that
everything is in its order

00:38:43.387 --> 00:38:45.856 align:start size:84% position:16%
and you talked about
the race aspect.

00:38:45.856 --> 00:38:47.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, one of the things
that was so appalling

00:38:47.725 --> 00:38:50.528
to me is what happened
with the Georgia bill.

00:38:50.528 --> 00:38:52.697 align:start size:84% position:16%
South Carolina when
I was governor,

00:38:52.697 --> 00:38:55.232
