00:44:17.388 --> 00:44:20.124
But what do you think
that that big chunk

00:44:20.124 --> 00:44:21.525
actually looks like?

00:44:21.525 --> 00:44:23.661 align:start size:97% position:3%
Like what kind of diversity
in a political sense

00:44:23.661 --> 00:44:24.595
can we get out of that?

00:44:24.595 --> 00:44:26.263
- So what I would like to think

00:44:26.263 --> 00:44:27.898 align:start size:84% position:16%
that the Republican
party will be,

00:44:27.898 --> 00:44:30.868
is it won't go back to
the party before Trump

00:44:30.868 --> 00:44:34.338 align:start size:97% position:3%
because that was a really
important move that we made.

00:44:34.338 --> 00:44:37.274 align:start position:0%
So many people like where I
grew up in rural South Carolina,

00:44:37.274 --> 00:44:42.112 align:start position:0%
who felt unheard, misunderstood,
not paid attention to,

00:44:42.112 --> 00:44:45.349 align:start position:0%
