00:45:38.802 --> 00:45:41.271 align:start size:84% position:16%
That means we're
doing something wrong.

00:45:41.271 --> 00:45:44.541
If we grow our tent,
if we grow our party

00:45:44.541 --> 00:45:46.643
we will be a stronger country

00:45:46.643 --> 00:45:48.345
and we will be able
to move the ball

00:45:48.345 --> 00:45:50.447 align:start size:84% position:16%
not for the next
presidential election,

00:45:50.447 --> 00:45:53.584
but for 20 and 30 years down
the road, we have to do it.

00:45:53.584 --> 00:45:56.019
- Do you think some of that
stuff can actually be healed?

00:45:56.019 --> 00:45:58.055 align:start size:97% position:3%
Like right now and you can't
judge things by Twitter

00:45:58.055 --> 00:45:59.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know that much, but
there does seem to be this

00:45:59.923 --> 00:46:03.627 align:start size:97% position:3%
like tension between whatever
the sort of MAGA camp is

00:46:03.627 --> 00:46:05.729
and then the pre-MAGA people

00:46:05.729 --> 00:46:07.431
and it's like how do
you get these people

00:46:07.431 --> 00:46:12.436
to kind of like you seem to
me to be like a synthesis

00:46:13.604 --> 00:46:14.872
of those things, but
like how do you do it?

00:46:14.872 --> 00:46:16.206
Because there seems to
be a lot of resentment

00:46:16.206 --> 00:46:18.208 align:start size:84% position:16%
from the MAGA people
to the old ones

00:46:18.208 --> 00:46:19.843
and then the old ones
to the MAGA of people

00:46:19.843 --> 00:46:21.345
and the whole thing.

00:46:21.345 --> 00:46:23.947 align:start size:97% position:3%
- I think the first thing
is the judgment has to stop.

00:46:23.947 --> 00:46:26.583
There's way too much
judgment of people.

00:46:26.583 --> 00:46:31.188
There's an unforgiving
side of just toxicity

00:46:32.122 --> 00:46:33.490
that's happening right now.

00:46:33.490 --> 00:46:35.692
And so what I think
we have to understand

00:46:35.692 --> 00:46:38.328
is everyday Joe Biden and
Kamala Harris are an office

00:46:38.328 --> 00:46:40.364 align:start size:84% position:16%
is another day we
should come together.

00:46:40.364 --> 00:46:42.299
But we are better together.

00:46:42.299 --> 00:46:45.536
You can fight each other all
you want, it is not productive.

00:46:45.536 --> 00:46:47.070
We are better together.

00:46:47.070 --> 00:46:49.706
We have a bigger enemy out
there and that's socialism

00:46:49.706 --> 00:46:52.843
and it's going to happen if we
sit there and keep fighting,

00:46:52.843 --> 00:46:54.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
all it's going to do is
open the door to socialism

00:46:54.845 --> 00:46:56.880 align:start position:0%
and we're going to end up
having to walk right through it.

00:46:56.880 --> 00:46:58.649
And then we won't have
time to go back and say,

00:46:58.649 --> 00:46:59.683
oh we should have.

00:46:59.683 --> 00:47:00.951
So come together.

00:47:00.951 --> 00:47:02.920
I respect both sides.

00:47:02.920 --> 00:47:07.424
It goes back to
in South Carolina

00:47:07.424 --> 00:47:09.760
when we removed the
Confederate flag.

00:47:09.760 --> 00:47:12.796 align:start size:97% position:3%
We had had a terrible
tragedy, it was a tough time

00:47:12.796 --> 00:47:15.465
and in that removal of
the Confederate flag,

00:47:15.465 --> 00:47:17.968
when I called for
it to be removed,

00:47:17.968 --> 00:47:20.037
I was very aware of two things,

00:47:20.037 --> 00:47:25.042 align:start size:97% position:3%
half of the state saw the
flag as heritage and ancestry.

00:47:26.243 --> 00:47:27.911
The other half of the
state saw it as hate.

00:47:27.911 --> 00:47:30.614
My job wasn't judge either side,

00:47:30.614 --> 00:47:33.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
my job was to get them
and move the ball forward.

00:47:33.851 --> 00:47:37.120 align:start size:81% position:19%
And so when you
take judgment out,

00:47:37.120 --> 00:47:39.923 align:start size:97% position:3%
then all of a sudden people's
defenses are not there,

00:47:39.923 --> 00:47:41.458
then they listen.

00:47:41.458 --> 00:47:43.994
And I worry right now that
there's a lot of judgment

00:47:43.994 --> 00:47:45.696
going back and forth.

00:47:45.696 --> 00:47:48.332 align:start size:88% position:13%
Don't shoot your sisters
and your brothers,

00:47:48.332 --> 00:47:49.833
we're in this together.

00:47:49.833 --> 00:47:51.668
We're one big family and
we've got to move forward

00:47:51.668 --> 00:47:54.104
but we move forward in
the conservative ideals

00:47:54.104 --> 00:47:55.606
that we all hold dear.

00:47:55.606 --> 00:47:57.875
We move forward because
we know socialism is bad,

00:47:57.875 --> 00:48:00.277
we move forward because we
know big government's bad,

00:48:00.277 --> 00:48:03.146 align:start size:97% position:3%
we move forward because
fiscal responsibility matters

00:48:03.146 --> 00:48:05.315 align:start size:88% position:13%
and all of those things
can work together

00:48:05.315 --> 00:48:07.117
if we're all on the same page.

00:48:07.117 --> 00:48:09.486
- What kind of pushed back did
you get from your own people

00:48:09.486 --> 00:48:12.322 align:start size:97% position:3%
when you started talking about
the flag after trial or so.

00:48:12.322 --> 00:48:14.057
- A lot. A lot.

00:48:15.225 --> 00:48:19.796 align:start size:84% position:16%
I think that anytime
you do something,

00:48:19.796 --> 00:48:21.965
you're never going to please a
hundred percent of the people

00:48:21.965 --> 00:48:23.767
and that can't be why you do it.

00:48:23.767 --> 00:48:26.670 align:start size:88% position:13%
You do it because you
can see something bigger

00:48:27.771 --> 00:48:30.440 align:start size:88% position:13%
and a better place
forward for all people.

00:48:30.440 --> 00:48:33.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, South Carolinians
there were many

00:48:33.110 --> 00:48:35.379
that were very upset
with me that I did that

00:48:35.379 --> 00:48:37.247
but at the end of the day,

00:48:37.247 --> 00:48:39.316
South Carolina is a
better state for it

00:48:39.316 --> 00:48:40.784
and they saw that afterwards.

00:48:40.784 --> 00:48:43.520
And we didn't have
riots, we had vigils,

00:48:43.520 --> 00:48:45.622 align:start size:84% position:16%
we didn't have
protests, we had hugs.

00:48:45.622 --> 00:48:48.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, we did it in a way
that the national media

00:48:48.992 --> 00:48:50.427
didn't tear us down.

00:48:50.427 --> 00:48:52.129
We did it in a way
that was respectful,

00:48:52.129 --> 00:48:53.997
We did it in a way
that moved the ball

00:48:53.997 --> 00:48:56.099
and that's what you have to do.

00:48:56.099 --> 00:48:59.803 align:start size:97% position:3%
There was another a month
prior to the church shooting,

00:48:59.803 --> 00:49:01.939
we had the shooting
of Walter Scott.

00:49:01.939 --> 00:49:05.642
Killed, shot seven times in
the back, unarmed black man.

00:49:05.642 --> 00:49:07.744
This was right after Ferguson.

00:49:07.744 --> 00:49:11.949
I just was so worried our
state would fall apart.

00:49:11.949 --> 00:49:14.418 align:start size:97% position:3%
The first thing I did was
called the Walter Scott family

00:49:14.418 --> 00:49:17.054
and say we will get
answers for you.

00:49:17.054 --> 00:49:18.622
If you will allow me this time

00:49:18.622 --> 00:49:20.457 align:start size:94% position:6%
I will get you everything
you need to know

00:49:20.457 --> 00:49:23.160 align:start size:88% position:13%
and we will make sure
his life wasn't in vain.

00:49:23.160 --> 00:49:25.495
The next call I made was
to law enforcement saying,

00:49:25.495 --> 00:49:28.999
we've got to fix this,
let's do this together.

00:49:28.999 --> 00:49:30.834 align:start size:81% position:19%
A month to the
day South Carolina

00:49:30.834 --> 00:49:33.070 align:start size:97% position:3%
passed the first body
camera bill in the country.

00:49:33.070 --> 00:49:34.838
And when I signed that bill,

00:49:34.838 --> 00:49:36.673 align:start size:81% position:19%
I had the Scott
family on one side

00:49:36.673 --> 00:49:39.576 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I said never again
will a dirty cop do

00:49:39.576 --> 00:49:41.979
to someone without
us having proof.

00:49:41.979 --> 00:49:43.814 align:start size:97% position:3%
And then I had law
enforcement on the other side

00:49:43.814 --> 00:49:45.983 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I said never
again will a good cop

00:49:45.983 --> 00:49:47.985
be accused of something bad.

00:49:49.152 --> 00:49:52.456
You have to be willing
to see the greater good

00:49:52.456 --> 00:49:53.890
and you have to be willing to...

00:49:53.890 --> 00:49:55.158
I mean, one leadership

00:49:55.158 --> 00:49:57.928
is not letting the two
sides kill each other,

00:49:57.928 --> 00:50:00.364 align:start size:84% position:16%
not letting the two
sides blame each other

00:50:00.364 --> 00:50:02.265
but getting the two
sides to understand

00:50:02.265 --> 00:50:04.668 align:start size:88% position:13%
we all are trying
better for better things

00:50:04.668 --> 00:50:06.670
and that means we all
got to give a little.

00:50:06.670 --> 00:50:09.039
- Do you think oddly that
a lot of the Democrats

00:50:09.039 --> 00:50:12.376 align:start position:0%
now are doing the complete
reverse which is sort of nodding

00:50:12.376 --> 00:50:14.411 align:start size:94% position:6%
to the violence that we're
seeing on the streets

00:50:14.411 --> 00:50:18.048
and they don't mind when
this chaos is erupted.

00:50:18.048 --> 00:50:19.616
- It's a real problem.

00:50:19.616 --> 00:50:22.619
When you go, it doesn't
make sense when you have

00:50:22.619 --> 00:50:26.323
these violent protests
and you're tearing down

00:50:26.323 --> 00:50:28.825 align:start size:84% position:16%
an African-American
small business

00:50:28.825 --> 00:50:32.129 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
or you're seeing
an African-American
police officer shot.

00:50:32.129 --> 00:50:34.698 line:0%
Like these things, you're
hurting your own people.

00:50:34.698 --> 00:50:36.800
I mean at the end of the day,
the protests and the violence,

00:50:36.800 --> 00:50:39.870
if you're upset I
get it, I get it.

00:50:39.870 --> 00:50:44.141
But do it productively in
a way that we move the ball

00:50:44.141 --> 00:50:47.611 align:start size:97% position:3%
because hurting the community,
whatever color you are,

00:50:47.611 --> 00:50:48.812
that's not moving the ball.

00:50:48.812 --> 00:50:50.280 align:start size:84% position:16%
That's only hurting
more people--

00:50:50.280 --> 00:50:51.548
- But are you shocked?

00:50:51.548 --> 00:50:52.816 align:start size:81% position:19%
Are you shocked
that no Democrats?

00:50:52.816 --> 00:50:54.584
I mean, really no.
Democrats are...

00:50:54.584 --> 00:50:57.120
Joe Biden is still only
saying Antifa is an idea,

00:50:58.622 --> 00:50:59.623
an idea that's caused about
$2 billion worth of damage.

00:50:59.623 --> 00:51:01.091
- Absolutely.

00:51:01.091 --> 00:51:04.828
No.I think that they fail to
see what they don't want to see

00:51:04.828 --> 00:51:07.264
and they immediately
judge and go after

00:51:07.264 --> 00:51:09.232 align:start size:84% position:16%
what they want to
assume as the culprit.

00:51:09.232 --> 00:51:12.335
And it's harmful for our country

00:51:12.335 --> 00:51:14.337
and something has to change.

00:51:14.337 --> 00:51:17.207 align:start size:88% position:13%
And our job is again,
not to sit back and say,

00:51:17.207 --> 00:51:19.443
it's done we can't do anything.

00:51:19.443 --> 00:51:22.112 align:start size:97% position:3%
No, you keep saying something,
you keep correcting them

00:51:22.112 --> 00:51:25.082 align:start size:97% position:3%
and do it unapologetically,
do it with courage,

00:51:25.082 --> 00:51:27.184 align:start size:84% position:16%
do it with strength
and do it with passion

00:51:27.184 --> 00:51:28.885
because when you do that,

00:51:28.885 --> 00:51:31.855 align:start size:97% position:3%
they don't have the standing
to really keep going.

00:51:31.855 --> 00:51:34.991
Because if you were to question
what's racist and what's not

00:51:34.991 --> 00:51:37.661
or question protests
and they can't say more

00:51:37.661 --> 00:51:39.162
than a second sentence

00:51:39.162 --> 00:51:41.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they have no other
explanation after that.

00:51:41.431 --> 00:51:44.000
- That's kind of why they're
into that censorship thing too.

00:51:44.000 --> 00:51:45.402
There's a little
something to that.

00:51:45.402 --> 00:51:47.404
So to that point, we
sorta touched on this

00:51:47.404 --> 00:51:51.575
but one of the reasons that I
came around on Trump was I saw

00:51:51.575 --> 00:51:53.777 align:start position:0%
that it wasn't just
Republicans fighting Democrats,

00:51:53.777 --> 00:51:56.346
it was Republicans versus
Democrats and the media.

00:51:56.346 --> 00:51:59.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he was just like,
I'm not going to take it.

00:51:59.082 --> 00:52:02.452 align:start size:97% position:3%
What do you think Republicans
can do in that fight?

00:52:02.452 --> 00:52:03.954
Because I get a lot.

00:52:03.954 --> 00:52:05.922
I hear a lot of people now
that are really regretting,

00:52:05.922 --> 00:52:08.792
my few good liberal friends
that are still talk to me,

00:52:08.792 --> 00:52:10.293
they're not happy with Biden.

00:52:10.293 --> 00:52:12.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
But what they're saying
is we still had to get rid

00:52:12.362 --> 00:52:15.565
of Trump because
of the way he spoke

00:52:15.565 --> 00:52:17.167
and all that kind of stuff.

00:52:17.167 --> 00:52:20.270
But to me, it was like, he
knew how to fight that thing

00:52:20.270 --> 00:52:23.206
and you're not going to get
the perfect guy to do that.

00:52:23.206 --> 00:52:24.941 align:start size:88% position:13%
Like, what do you think
Republicans can do?

00:52:24.941 --> 00:52:27.077 align:start size:97% position:3%
Like you can see them doing
this with DeSantis now though,

00:52:27.077 --> 00:52:29.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
that awful 60 minutes
hit piece and everything.

00:52:29.212 --> 00:52:31.148
I was like what do
you think Republicans

00:52:31.148 --> 00:52:32.849
can do in that arena?

00:52:32.849 --> 00:52:33.917
Because that's not
the political arena,

00:52:33.917 --> 00:52:34.851
that's more the media arena.

00:52:34.851 --> 00:52:36.353
- I mean, I think we've seen...

00:52:36.353 --> 00:52:38.722 align:start size:97% position:3%
Look, I've been hit recently
by a liberal reporter

00:52:38.722 --> 00:52:40.690
that will go out and
they'll do profiles

00:52:40.690 --> 00:52:42.459 align:start size:84% position:16%
and they'll try
and shoot you down.

00:52:43.627 --> 00:52:44.494
- Are you talking about
that political piece?

00:52:44.494 --> 00:52:45.629
I read it this morning.

00:52:47.264 --> 00:52:49.933 align:start size:84% position:16%
I don't want to give
them the clicks,

00:52:49.933 --> 00:52:51.468
but I read it this morning.

00:52:51.468 --> 00:52:54.237
The first paragraph alone,
well first of it's fiction.

00:52:54.237 --> 00:52:56.072 align:start size:84% position:16%
They actually write
it as a fiction story.

00:52:56.072 --> 00:52:58.875
- There were so many
untruths in that story

00:52:58.875 --> 00:53:01.611
but that was meant
to be a hit job.

00:53:01.611 --> 00:53:02.913
They knew exactly...

00:53:02.913 --> 00:53:05.081
It didn't matter what I said,

00:53:05.081 --> 00:53:07.250
they wanted to fit it
into their narrative.

00:53:07.250 --> 00:53:09.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's what the media
does is they take it

00:53:09.719 --> 00:53:11.321
and they've already
got the story written

00:53:11.321 --> 00:53:12.923
before you say the first word.

00:53:12.923 --> 00:53:15.492
And what we have to
do is call it out

00:53:15.492 --> 00:53:18.828
and say this is a lie,
this is wrong, whatever.

00:53:18.828 --> 00:53:20.530
But boy, we have to
keep pushing back

00:53:20.530 --> 00:53:23.066 align:start size:88% position:13%
and again, that's why
the media is not trusted

00:53:23.066 --> 00:53:24.668
but it's a real problem.

00:53:24.668 --> 00:53:27.837 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's a problem because
there's more liberal outlets

00:53:27.837 --> 00:53:29.639 align:start size:84% position:16%
than there are
conservative outlets.

00:53:29.639 --> 00:53:31.107
And so the liberal outlets,

00:53:31.107 --> 00:53:33.410 align:start size:84% position:16%
anyone that they think
is starting to rise

00:53:33.410 --> 00:53:35.679 align:start size:97% position:3%
or get a louder voice, they're
going to shoot you down

00:53:35.679 --> 00:53:37.047
and they're going to
find some way to do it.

00:53:37.047 --> 00:53:38.348
- I don't want to
link to the piece

00:53:38.348 --> 00:53:39.950
but maybe we'll put an
image up or something

00:53:39.950 --> 00:53:42.752
from the piece because
it was so extraordinary.

00:53:42.752 --> 00:53:43.987 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's literally
written as fiction.

00:53:43.987 --> 00:53:47.490
- It's the worst and
the amazing thing is--

00:53:47.490 --> 00:53:49.125 align:start size:84% position:16%
- It's hard to really
make me be like,

00:53:49.125 --> 00:53:51.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
whoa at this point because
I've been through it,

00:53:51.027 --> 00:53:52.562
but like I was--

00:53:52.562 --> 00:53:55.432
- Not only that 95% of what
I said about Trump was good

00:53:55.432 --> 00:53:58.635
and he was angry about
it, he was mad about it.

00:53:58.635 --> 00:54:01.671 align:start size:84% position:16%
And then the 5%
that I said related,

00:54:01.671 --> 00:54:03.807 align:start size:84% position:16%
they acted like I woke
up with an epiphany

00:54:03.807 --> 00:54:05.308
that something happened.

00:54:05.308 --> 00:54:08.678 align:start size:97% position:3%
The problem with articles
like that is they are trying

00:54:08.678 --> 00:54:11.781
to change the political
dynamic on their own.

00:54:11.781 --> 00:54:14.284
They're trying to create
the story on their own

00:54:14.284 --> 00:54:16.786 align:start size:97% position:3%
because they know the
Democrats don't have a bench.

00:54:16.786 --> 00:54:18.888
They know that they don't
have strength behind them.

00:54:18.888 --> 00:54:20.257
So they think the best
way to do it is just

00:54:20.257 --> 00:54:23.159
tear everybody down and
do it in different ways.

00:54:23.159 --> 00:54:25.295
And we're watching it happen
to all of our Republicans.

00:54:25.295 --> 00:54:27.097
They'll just tear you
down one at a time.

00:54:27.097 --> 00:54:28.698
They'll find some way to do it.

00:54:28.698 --> 00:54:31.401
And I don't know
what the answer is,

00:54:31.401 --> 00:54:33.837
I just know that we don't
cave, we keep fighting.

00:54:33.837 --> 00:54:36.106 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Do you think that
basically conservatives

00:54:36.106 --> 00:54:37.841 align:start size:97% position:3%
and again I mean that in
sort of the wide sense of it,

00:54:37.841 --> 00:54:40.443 align:start size:97% position:3%
just have to start building
completely new things.

00:54:40.443 --> 00:54:41.811 align:start size:81% position:19%
I mean, this is
sort of a new idea

00:54:41.811 --> 00:54:43.346
that's out there
now which is like,

00:54:43.346 --> 00:54:45.915
in essence conservatives will
have to have their own banks,

00:54:45.915 --> 00:54:48.318
they'll have to have their
own places of journalism,

00:54:48.318 --> 00:54:50.787
they'll have to have their
own educational institutions,

00:54:50.787 --> 00:54:54.991
that at some level these things
are just irreparably damaged

00:54:54.991 --> 00:54:56.259
and we should just
let them have it

00:54:56.259 --> 00:54:58.295
and the rest of us will
build better things.

00:54:58.295 --> 00:55:00.864
- I mean, I don't know that
it's irreparably damaged.

00:55:00.864 --> 00:55:03.466 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, I think that the
media misses Trump terribly.

00:55:03.466 --> 00:55:04.901
I think they're so bored.

00:55:04.901 --> 00:55:06.836
I mean, I was in the
airport the other day

00:55:06.836 --> 00:55:08.938 align:start size:88% position:13%
and a reporters chasing
me down the airport

00:55:08.938 --> 00:55:11.174
and I'm like, this
is what have left.

00:55:11.174 --> 00:55:14.377
I think that the idea is
they miss his tweeting,

00:55:14.377 --> 00:55:17.480
they miss the stories because
it provided something everyday

00:55:17.480 --> 00:55:19.416 align:start size:84% position:16%
and their ratings
went through the roof.

00:55:19.416 --> 00:55:21.184
Now their ratings are not
going through the roof.

00:55:21.184 --> 00:55:23.320
People are watching less news
because they're tired of it,

00:55:23.320 --> 00:55:26.089
people are not getting
as much benefit from it

00:55:26.089 --> 00:55:27.357
because there's no substance,

00:55:27.357 --> 00:55:29.793
it's more opinion
than it is facts.

00:55:29.793 --> 00:55:31.294
And I think people are done

00:55:31.294 --> 00:55:35.065
but I do think conservatives
should support conservatives.

00:55:35.065 --> 00:55:39.869
Whether it's businesses,
whether it's media outlets,

00:55:39.869 --> 00:55:41.104
whether it's something else

00:55:41.104 --> 00:55:42.572 align:start size:81% position:19%
or whether it's
creating your own,

00:55:42.572 --> 00:55:44.808
is don't feel like you
have to deal with it,

00:55:44.808 --> 00:55:47.344
let's find ways to make
our own side better.

00:55:47.344 --> 00:55:48.845
Let's find ways to fix it.

00:55:48.845 --> 00:55:51.915
- So when I've talked to my,
let's say left leaning friends,

00:55:51.915 --> 00:55:53.750 align:start size:84% position:16%
about this new
conservative movement,

00:55:53.750 --> 00:55:55.652
the two that still get them,

00:55:55.652 --> 00:55:59.089
it's always the same two
it's abortion and belief

00:55:59.089 --> 00:56:00.290
that most of them come.

00:56:00.290 --> 00:56:02.492
Not that they're
all purely atheists

00:56:02.492 --> 00:56:03.860
but they have this
real thing about,

00:56:03.860 --> 00:56:06.162
oh, the right it's
just too religious

00:56:06.162 --> 00:56:07.130
or something like that.

00:56:07.130 --> 00:56:08.998
So could you kind of sue them

00:56:08.998 --> 00:56:10.467
perhaps on either one of those?

00:56:10.467 --> 00:56:14.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
My example, I'll just
tell you is Rudy Giuliani

00:56:14.237 --> 00:56:15.939
is obviously a conservative

00:56:15.939 --> 00:56:17.974 align:start size:84% position:16%
and he was obviously
a Trump supporter

00:56:17.974 --> 00:56:19.476
and not only when
he got divorced,

00:56:19.476 --> 00:56:21.277
oh because then they'll also
say the gay thing a little bit

00:56:21.277 --> 00:56:22.812 align:start size:84% position:16%
which I think the ship
has sailed on that,

00:56:22.812 --> 00:56:25.415
well, he lived with two gay
guys after he got divorced,

00:56:25.415 --> 00:56:27.917
he's pro choice and he
was a Trump supporter

00:56:27.917 --> 00:56:30.720 align:start position:0%
so it's like, nobody's doubting
that he's a conservative,

00:56:30.720 --> 00:56:33.690
so I see a wider tent there.

00:56:33.690 --> 00:56:34.958
What would you say about that?

00:56:34.958 --> 00:56:37.227
- Look, I mean I think
we all have our views

00:56:37.227 --> 00:56:40.697
and I think again, lack
of judgment is important

00:56:40.697 --> 00:56:42.198
as you go for.

00:56:42.198 --> 00:56:44.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just don't believe in
being a judgmental person,

00:56:44.601 --> 00:56:47.771
I don't think anybody
else should allow them

00:56:47.771 --> 00:56:49.839 align:start size:88% position:13%
to go into that
negative energy either.

00:56:49.839 --> 00:56:52.175 align:start size:84% position:16%
But look, I mean
conservatives are...

00:56:52.175 --> 00:56:54.110
I'm a person of deep faith

00:56:54.110 --> 00:56:57.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think that God has
blessed us in so many ways

00:56:57.781 --> 00:57:02.719 align:start size:97% position:3%
but I use mine as it's like
my parents always said,

00:57:04.087 --> 00:57:05.622 align:start position:0%
the best way to appreciate
your blessings is to give back.

00:57:05.622 --> 00:57:08.057
So it's more of like a
service that you feel

00:57:08.057 --> 00:57:09.559
that you give back.

00:57:09.559 --> 00:57:11.761 align:start size:97% position:3%
If you've been blessed with
goods, you try and pass it on,

00:57:11.761 --> 00:57:12.962
you try and hold
the ladder down,

00:57:12.962 --> 00:57:14.330
you try and help other people

00:57:14.330 --> 00:57:18.501 align:start size:88% position:13%
and you know that
there's a higher power.

00:57:18.501 --> 00:57:21.771
Some people don't believe
in that and that's okay.

00:57:21.771 --> 00:57:25.408 align:start position:0%
That's not something that I
would ever judge someone for it.

00:57:25.408 --> 00:57:26.876
Same thing with the pro-life.

00:57:26.876 --> 00:57:29.813
I'm pro-life not because the
Republican party tells me to be

00:57:29.813 --> 00:57:31.514 align:start size:84% position:16%
but because my
husband was adopted

00:57:31.514 --> 00:57:33.783 align:start size:81% position:19%
and I'm blessed
every day for him.

00:57:33.783 --> 00:57:37.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I think experiences
are what form us

00:57:37.520 --> 00:57:38.755
but at the end of the day

00:57:38.755 --> 00:57:40.690
we have to look at
the greater good

00:57:40.690 --> 00:57:42.792
and figure out how we get there.

00:57:42.792 --> 00:57:47.497
And so I also don't think
we're all one issue people.

00:57:47.497 --> 00:57:49.899 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, the way the
Democrats always assume women

00:57:49.899 --> 00:57:52.669 align:start size:84% position:16%
are so divided on
the pro-choice issue.

00:57:52.669 --> 00:57:53.870
- They are so for women

00:57:53.870 --> 00:57:55.772 align:start size:88% position:13%
but I always say they're
not for Nikki Haley.

00:57:55.772 --> 00:57:58.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
There are so for women,
they are for black people,

00:57:58.141 --> 00:57:59.576
they're not for Candace Owens.

00:57:59.576 --> 00:58:01.845 align:start size:97% position:3%
- I mean, my thing is
like, that's just ludicrous

00:58:01.845 --> 00:58:05.281
to think that one issue
should make or break us.

00:58:05.281 --> 00:58:07.584
I don't agree with my husband
a hundred percent of the time,

00:58:07.584 --> 00:58:09.586 align:start size:81% position:19%
it doesn't mean
that I don't love.

00:58:09.586 --> 00:58:13.456 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I think that anytime they
try and one issue us off,

00:58:13.456 --> 00:58:15.892 align:start size:88% position:13%
that's again
desperation to do that.

00:58:15.892 --> 00:58:18.828
- Do you think part of this
is sort of just the politics

00:58:18.828 --> 00:58:21.798 align:start size:84% position:16%
as religion that
something has shifted

00:58:21.798 --> 00:58:24.367
in the way we talk
about politics now

00:58:24.367 --> 00:58:26.870
that everything is
political everywhere.

00:58:26.870 --> 00:58:28.638
I don't watch, I got a
basketball behind me,

00:58:28.638 --> 00:58:31.174 align:start size:97% position:3%
I don't watch the NBA
anymore because I couldn't.

00:58:31.174 --> 00:58:32.775
Partly was because
of the China thing.

00:58:32.775 --> 00:58:35.078
I'm watching LeBron won't
say a word about China

00:58:35.078 --> 00:58:39.716 align:start size:97% position:3%
and they have Black Lives
Matter on the court and yeah.

00:58:39.716 --> 00:58:41.217
What do you think about that?

00:58:41.217 --> 00:58:44.787
- I think politics has gotten
too involved in everything.

00:58:44.787 --> 00:58:47.323
And that's the thing
is I feel like it's all

00:58:47.323 --> 00:58:50.293 align:start size:97% position:3%
about soundbites and it's
not about substance anymore.

00:58:50.293 --> 00:58:53.429
So people are just spouting
off things that are hateful.

00:58:53.429 --> 00:58:55.431 align:start size:84% position:16%
I don't know if COVID
exacerbated that,

00:58:55.431 --> 00:58:58.234
I don't know whether it's
social media that's done it

00:58:58.234 --> 00:59:01.170
but people are so quick
to say hateful things

00:59:01.170 --> 00:59:02.939
but they won't do
it in person yet,

00:59:04.107 --> 00:59:05.308
but they will do it
through the media.

00:59:05.308 --> 00:59:06.943
- If you got one of this.

00:59:06.943 --> 00:59:09.279
- They'll do it in
every other way.

00:59:09.279 --> 00:59:11.447
So I do hope that calms down.

00:59:11.447 --> 00:59:14.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean politics should
never be a hundred percent

00:59:14.183 --> 00:59:15.385
of anyone's life.

00:59:17.287 --> 00:59:20.089 align:start size:97% position:3%
Politics for a lot of
years may have been my job,

00:59:20.089 --> 00:59:21.491
but I never took it home.

00:59:21.491 --> 00:59:22.992 align:start size:84% position:16%
I have friends
that are Democrats,

00:59:22.992 --> 00:59:25.528
I have friends that have
different views than I do,

00:59:25.528 --> 00:59:28.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
I watch movies with
actors that are Democrats,

00:59:28.631 --> 00:59:30.667 line:0%
I'm not one of those that
says you can only listen

00:59:30.667 --> 00:59:33.269 line:0%
to conservative musicians.

00:59:33.269 --> 00:59:36.172
I appreciate all
of those things.

00:59:36.172 --> 00:59:38.041
I think there's a
place for politics

00:59:38.041 --> 00:59:40.176
and I think that's
at the voting booth.

00:59:40.176 --> 00:59:41.711 align:start size:81% position:19%
And I think that's
in making sure

00:59:41.711 --> 00:59:44.047 align:start size:84% position:16%
that you're supporting
candidates and
that's making sure

00:59:44.047 --> 00:59:45.915
that you're moving
the ball on policy

00:59:45.915 --> 00:59:47.850
but the rest don't forget
to love your neighbor.

00:59:47.850 --> 00:59:49.319
It still matters.

00:59:49.319 --> 00:59:51.888 align:start position:0%
- Gosh, I really forgot how
much I love just sitting across

00:59:51.888 --> 00:59:54.190
from somebody and not staring
into a screen all the time.

00:59:54.190 --> 00:59:57.827
So before I ask you the
one that you probably

00:59:57.827 --> 00:59:59.829 align:start size:88% position:13%
don't want to be asked,
the last question,

00:59:59.829 --> 01:00:01.531 align:start size:88% position:13%
I didn't look at my
notes this entire time.

01:00:01.531 --> 01:00:02.899
I was with you the whole time,

01:00:02.899 --> 01:00:04.200
is there anything
else that you want

01:00:04.200 --> 01:00:06.736
to get off your chest
perhaps at the moment?

01:00:06.736 --> 01:00:08.271 align:start size:84% position:16%
Anything else
that's on your mind

01:00:08.271 --> 01:00:10.106
before I get to that question
that you know I'm going to ask

01:00:10.106 --> 01:00:11.774 align:start size:84% position:16%
that you probably
don't want me to ask.

01:00:11.774 --> 01:00:14.877
- No. I just I want everybody
to remember how blessed we are

01:00:14.877 --> 01:00:18.247
and we've just gone through
what was a traumatic year.

01:00:19.415 --> 01:00:21.985
From school closings
to masking, to deaths,

01:00:21.985 --> 01:00:24.587
to everything in between.

01:00:24.587 --> 01:00:27.290
But that doesn't mean we
have to sink down with it,

01:00:27.290 --> 01:00:29.559 align:start size:84% position:16%
I think we can
rise up above that.

01:00:29.559 --> 01:00:32.895
If we just showed how
resilient we are again,

01:00:32.895 --> 01:00:35.698
we just showed that it
Operation Warp Speed

01:00:35.698 --> 01:00:38.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they found a vaccine
in less than a year.

01:00:38.134 --> 01:00:40.870
We just showed the goodness
of our first responders.

01:00:40.870 --> 01:00:44.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like so much good and
blessings came out of it,

01:00:44.374 --> 01:00:47.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
take that energy and
let's carry that forward.

01:00:47.276 --> 01:00:49.612
Don't let all of this negativity

01:00:49.612 --> 01:00:50.947 align:start size:81% position:19%
and everything
else bring us down

01:00:50.947 --> 01:00:53.116
because we've got a
lot of work to do.

01:00:53.116 --> 01:00:54.384
- That could have
been the closing--

01:00:54.384 --> 01:00:55.284
- 2022 we got a
lot of work to do

01:00:55.284 --> 01:00:56.753
- Ah, 2022.

01:00:56.753 --> 01:00:59.589 align:start size:97% position:3%
I want to talk about two
years after that for a second.

01:00:59.589 --> 01:01:02.291
You know I have to
ask, I have to ask.

01:01:02.291 --> 01:01:05.528
Come on, come on, give me
something, it'll go viral.

01:01:05.528 --> 01:01:07.497
- I just don't think I have
to make that decision yet.

01:01:07.497 --> 01:01:08.431
I don't, I don't.

01:01:08.431 --> 01:01:10.466
I think that the way I look at

01:01:10.466 --> 01:01:12.869 align:start size:94% position:6%
is I've never been one
that's thought too far out

01:01:12.869 --> 01:01:16.039
but I do think 2022
really important.

01:01:16.039 --> 01:01:19.042
We have to win the house, I
think we can win the Senate,

01:01:19.042 --> 01:01:21.344
I'm an optimist, we've got
to win some governor's races.

01:01:21.344 --> 01:01:24.280
We've got Virginia and
New Jersey up this year.

01:01:24.280 --> 01:01:26.716
And so I think there's a
lot of work to be done.

01:01:26.716 --> 01:01:30.119
I think that I don't have to
make a decision before then

01:01:30.119 --> 01:01:31.721 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I think afterwards
we'll kind of see

01:01:31.721 --> 01:01:33.389
where the chips fall,

01:01:33.389 --> 01:01:36.259
but it's not something
that I grew up saying,

01:01:36.259 --> 01:01:37.827
oh, I have to do this.

01:01:37.827 --> 01:01:39.128
No, I have a family.

01:01:39.128 --> 01:01:41.497
You think twice about it
when you have a family,

01:01:41.497 --> 01:01:44.000
you think twice about it
when you know other people

01:01:44.000 --> 01:01:46.102
will be affected and it's not.

01:01:46.102 --> 01:01:48.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
Politics is a blood sport,
it's not fun right now.

01:01:48.738 --> 01:01:50.807
It's a tough time to be in it.

01:01:50.807 --> 01:01:53.009
But right now I feel like
I can do the greatest good

01:01:53.009 --> 01:01:54.944
by making sure we win the
house in the Senate back.

01:01:54.944 --> 01:01:56.813
And so we're campaigning here,

01:01:56.813 --> 01:01:58.548 align:start size:97% position:3%
we're going to be campaigning
for Michelle Steele

01:01:58.548 --> 01:02:02.685 align:start size:97% position:3%
and Young Kim, we've endorsed
Marionette Miller-Meeks

01:02:02.685 --> 01:02:04.687
and Julia Letlow from Louisiana,

01:02:04.687 --> 01:02:06.823 align:start position:0%
we're going to be helping
candidates all over the country

01:02:06.823 --> 01:02:08.725
and we're going to try and
recruit some really good ones

01:02:08.725 --> 01:02:13.296
because the ones that won in
this past congressional races,

01:02:13.296 --> 01:02:15.598
man, they're good
quality people.

01:02:15.598 --> 01:02:17.100 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, they are
going to run circles

01:02:17.100 --> 01:02:20.169
around Nancy Pelosi and
we need more of that.

01:02:20.169 --> 01:02:21.104
- All right.

01:02:21.104 --> 01:02:23.573
Well, ambassador, governor,

01:02:23.573 --> 01:02:25.541 align:start size:88% position:13%
undeclared
presidential candidate.

01:02:25.541 --> 01:02:26.576
- It's Nikki.

01:02:26.576 --> 01:02:28.077
Those are moments and times

01:02:28.077 --> 01:02:29.312
- It was a pleasure.

01:02:29.312 --> 01:02:30.747 align:start size:84% position:16%
It was just so nice
so nice talking to you

01:02:30.747 --> 01:02:32.415
and actually seeing
the person again.

01:02:32.415 --> 01:02:33.716 align:start size:88% position:13%
- This was a great time.
Thanks for having me.

01:02:33.716 --> 01:02:35.184
- Well, thank you so much.

01:02:35.184 --> 01:02:38.087 align:start position:0%
We are not going to link to
that political piece down below

01:02:38.087 --> 01:02:42.925
but we will link to Nikki's
book, "With All Due Respect",

01:02:42.925 --> 01:02:44.360
which I've got right here

01:02:44.360 --> 01:02:45.828
and we'll do more
of these in person.

